moment today - maybe when you\'re texting a friend or joining a group chat - and use that phrase before you hit send? I\'m curious to hear how it feels when you try it.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Ok. I will try it.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m really glad you\'re willing to try this. What\'s one thing that comes to mind when you think about using this phrase? It\'s okay if it\'s small or even if it feels hard to share right now.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Maybe it doesnt work...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kimberly, it\'s completely normal to wonder if it\'ll work - that\'s part of the process. What if we think of it as gathering information instead? Even if it doesn\'t feel perfect, you\'re still learning what helps you most. How does that shift your perspective?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah, i would like to know what could really help me not feel anxious when i\'m with other people... '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kimberly, I love that you\'re looking for what works for you. What if we try something small today - like noticing one thing you did well in a social interaction, even if it felt awkward? We can build from there.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I think i do a lot of things well. The problem is that... for example, i\'ll lie in bed thinking through conversations... sometimes i wake up at night and cant stop thinking how i could have said something different.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kimberly, it\'s really helpful that you\'re noticing how these thoughts connect to your daytime experiences. What if we tried one small experiment tonight: when you catch yourself ruminating, instead of analyzing past conversations, you gently shift to asking ""What\'s one thing I could try differently tomorrow?"" Would you be open to testing that?'}, {'role': user, 'content': But how can i stop having these thoughts and doubting myself all the time...?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kimberly, I know how draining it feels to have these thoughts loop endlessly. While we can\'t magically stop them, what if we tried a small experiment: when you notice doubting thoughts, gently pause and ask ""What\'s one small step I could take right now that would make me feel a bit more confident?"" This shifts from analyzing past interactions to taking action in the present. Would you be open to trying this for just one conversation this week?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'But if i knew wich step would be that, i wouldnt be here talking to you...'}]","But if i knew wich step would be that, i wouldnt be here talking to you...",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
