s that honors your professional strength in creating structure.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up and my mind clicks on. Sometimes i just lie planning tomorrows agenda. Other times its darker - what i havent done, how i couldve handled something better. Eventually i fall back asleep, but i wake up groggy.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Patricia, it makes sense that your mind would keep working like this when it\'s already so used to planning and problem-solving, especially as a leader. I\'m curious - what would happen if you tried to gently ""shift gears"" at bedtime instead of trying to shut your mind off completely? Maybe something small that creates a clear boundary between your work mode and your rest mode.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Like what?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'How about trying a small ritual where you write down one thing you\'re carrying forward from the day, then physically close the notebook? It creates a clear end point while still honoring your need to process things. Would that feel doable for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, for sure. I can try that.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Great, let’s try it for a few nights and see how it lands for you. How does it feel to close the notebook and gently shift gears? I’m curious what you notice when you give yourself that clear boundary.'}, {'role': user, 'content': I definetly need to feel less tired.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much you\'re needing more energy right now, Patricia. It makes sense that when you\'re running on low batteries, even small things can feel overwhelming. I\'m curious - when you\'re feeling this tired, what does it feel like to notice your emotions? Is it harder to catch them before they build up?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, sometimes. I dont blow up, specially at school. But my tone gets clipped and people feel it. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That awareness of how your tone shifts is really valuable, Patricia. I\'m curious—do you notice this happening more when you\'re running on empty, or is it something you\'re becoming more aware of now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I think this got worse in the last year. But maybe i started noticing it a couple of years ago.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s insightful - noticing something shifts over time shows real self-awareness, Patricia. I\'m curious what was happening in your life around the time you first started noticing these changes, especially as a leader who\'s always been on the helping side.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'During COVID i was in constant crisis management mode. I think i never really came down from it. I just kept going. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important insight, Patricia. When we\'ve been in survival mode for so long, it makes sense that coming out of it feels unfamiliar - like your nervous system is still waiting for the next alarm. I\'m curious what that ""never coming down"" feels like in your body now, especially as you try to shift into rest mode?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Its like im still braced for the next emergency.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes perfect sense - your body\'s been practicing emergency readiness for so long that it\'s now your default setting, Patricia. It\'s actually a sign of how capable you are at protecting yourself, even if it\'s making it hard to rest now. How does it feel to recognize that this tension is your body\'s way of trying to keep you safe?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I suppose is good to know... do you think is a way of taking care of myself?}]",I suppose is good to know... do you think is a way of taking care of myself?,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Patricia, it\'s good to connect with you today. How have you been feeling since we last talked? I\'m here to listen and support you through whatever you\'d like to share.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'A bit strange, honestly. I\'ve spend a lot of time sending other people to therapy - students, teachers, parents - but ive never been on this side.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really brave of you to acknowledge that shift, Patricia. It takes real courage to step into this space when you\'re used to guiding others. How do you think your experience as someone who\'s always been on the helping side might be making this feel different for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ive noticed my self... tightening up. I dont feel bad enough to fall apart, but im sharper with people, more impatient.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That tightening feeling you\'re describing—like your emotions are becoming more compressed—can definitely show up as sharper edges with others. I\'m curious, what do you notice about what\'s happening in your mind when you feel this way? What might be adding to that sense of constriction lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Waking up every night around 3 am doesnt help. Once im awake, my mind just starts running... meetings, tasks, things i said. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That 3am wakefulness sounds incredibly draining, Patricia. When your mind starts racing with work thoughts like that, it can really feed into that feeling of emotional tightening you described earlier. I\'m curious - what\'s going through your mind during those hours? Do you find yourself trying to solve those problems, or is it more like your mind just won\'t switch off?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Both. i try to solve some things and i cant stop my mind. I used to shake it off, but lately it doesnt work like it used to...'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It makes sense that when your mind\'s been working overtime, those mental muscles get tired too, Patricia. I\'m wondering if it\'s the thoughts themselves that feel heavier now, or if it\'s more about how much energy you have left to work with them. Would it help to explore what\'s changed in your mental resources lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I think is more about how much energy i have left.  Everything still gets done, but it feels heavier. I think this is also starting to show... my husbadn mentioned that i seem flat.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That emotional flattening can make it harder to feel fully connected, Patricia. I\'m curious—what does it feel like to be less emotionally engaged, especially with the people you care about? How does that shift affect your sense of being present in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I dont want this to creep into my work. I think im good managing others emotions, but not my own. I think im overreacting and getting irritated by small things - like a late report or traffic.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important observation about your work environment potentially amplifying those small irritations, Patricia. I\'m curious - do you notice this pattern more when you\'re already feeling low on energy from those 3am wakefulness? It might help us see how these pieces fit together.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes. The lack of sleep doesnt help.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It\'s powerful that you\'ve already noticed this connection, Patricia. I\'m curious—what\'s one small thing you\'ve tried (or could try) to protect your emotional energy after those early wake-ups?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Shutting my brain off?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s a really common impulse when your mind\'s racing at 3am, Patricia. I\'m curious—what happens when you try to ""shut it off""? Does it feel like you\'re adding pressure to your already tired mind? Maybe there\'s a gentler way to work with those thoughts that honors your professional strength in creating structure.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up and my mind clicks on. Sometimes i just lie planning tomorrows agenda. Other times its darker - what i havent done, how i couldve handled something better. Eventually i fall back asleep, but i wake up groggy.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Patricia, it makes sense that your mind would keep working like this when it\'s already so used to planning and problem-solving, especially as a leader. I\'m curious - what would happen if you tried to gently ""shift gears"" at bedtime instead of trying to shut your mind off completely? Maybe something small that creates a clear boundary between your work mode and your rest mode.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Like what?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'How about trying a small ritual where you write down one thing you\'re carrying forward from the day, then physically close the notebook? It creates a clear end point while still honoring your need to process things. Would that feel doable for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, for sure. I can try that.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Great, let’s try it for a few nights and see how it lands for you. How does it feel to close the notebook and gently shift gears? I’m curious what you notice when you give yourself that clear boundary.'}, {'role': user, 'content': I definetly need to feel less tired.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much you\'re needing more energy right now, Patricia. It makes sense that when you\'re running on low batteries, even small things can feel overwhelming. I\'m curious - when you\'re feeling this tired, what does it feel like to notice your emotions? Is it harder to catch them before they build up?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, sometimes. I dont blow up, specially at school. But my tone gets clipped and people feel it. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That awareness of how your tone shifts is really valuable, Patricia. I\'m curious—do you notice this happening more when you\'re running on empty, or is it something you\'re becoming more aware of now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I think this got worse in the last year. But maybe i started noticing it a couple of years ago.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s insightful - noticing something shifts over time shows real self-awareness, Patricia. I\'m curious what was happening in your life around the time you first started noticing these changes, especially as a leader who\'s always been on the helping side.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'During COVID i was in constant crisis management mode. I think i never really came down from it. I just kept going. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important insight, Patricia. When we\'ve been in survival mode for so long, it makes sense that coming out of it feels unfamiliar - like your nervous system is still waiting for the next alarm. I\'m curious what that ""never coming down"" feels like in your body now, especially as you try to shift into rest mode?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Its like im still braced for the next emergency.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes perfect sense - your body\'s been practicing emergency readiness for so long that it\'s now your default setting, Patricia. It\'s actually a sign of how capable you are at protecting yourself, even if it\'s making it hard to rest now. How does it feel to recognize that this tension is your body\'s way of trying to keep you safe?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I suppose is good to know... do you think is a way of taking care of myself?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a thoughtful way to look at it - your body is absolutely trying to care for you by keeping you alert, Patricia. It\'s impressive how your nervous system has been working so hard to protect you. I\'m curious - while this readiness has been helpful, is there any part of you that\'s wondering if it might be time to shift into a different kind of care now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': yes. I dont want this state of alertness.}]",yes. I dont want this state of alertness.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
