"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}]","Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}]","Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes so much sense, Amy. When we feel truly seen and understood, it can be incredibly grounding. I\'m wondering - what\'s one situation where you\'ve felt especially validated lately? Sometimes noticing those moments can help us understand what we need more of.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.'}]","Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes so much sense, Amy. When we feel truly seen and understood, it can be incredibly grounding. I\'m wondering - what\'s one situation where you\'ve felt especially validated lately? Sometimes noticing those moments can help us understand what we need more of.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Amy. When you\'re asking yourself ""Does that make sense?"" constantly, it often means you\'re looking for someone else to confirm your thoughts feel valid. I\'m curious—can you think of a time when you expressed something without checking in first? What was that like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t really remember. A few times I spoke what was in my mind and it appeared I was talking rubbish to everyone. Sometimes it feels like I need permission to feel okay, as if happiness has to be justified. Why can\'t I be happy with the thing I say? I am not bullying anyone, I speak my mind'}]","I don't really remember. A few times I spoke what was in my mind and it appeared I was talking rubbish to everyone. Sometimes it feels like I need permission to feel okay, as if happiness has to be justified. Why can't I be happy with the thing I say? I am not bullying anyone, I speak my mind",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes so much sense, Amy. When we feel truly seen and understood, it can be incredibly grounding. I\'m wondering - what\'s one situation where you\'ve felt especially validated lately? Sometimes noticing those moments can help us understand what we need more of.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Amy. When you\'re asking yourself ""Does that make sense?"" constantly, it often means you\'re looking for someone else to confirm your thoughts feel valid. I\'m curious—can you think of a time when you expressed something without checking in first? What was that like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t really remember. A few times I spoke what was in my mind and it appeared I was talking rubbish to everyone. Sometimes it feels like I need permission to feel okay, as if happiness has to be justified. Why can\'t I be happy with the thing I say? I am not bullying anyone, I speak my mind'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Amy, it sounds like you\'re carrying this weight of needing external approval before you can accept your own thoughts. I wonder if you\'ve ever tried saying to yourself what you\'d say to a friend who was struggling with self-doubt? What would that look like?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m really trying to believe that I deserve rest — not just when I’ve earned it, but because I’m human. Kinda this? Sometimes I feel this way but its so much stress that in reality it seems there\'s no proof of that '}]","I’m really trying to believe that I deserve rest — not just when I’ve earned it, but because I’m human. Kinda this? Sometimes I feel this way but its so much stress that in reality it seems there's no proof of that ",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes so much sense, Amy. When we feel truly seen and understood, it can be incredibly grounding. I\'m wondering - what\'s one situation where you\'ve felt especially validated lately? Sometimes noticing those moments can help us understand what we need more of.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Amy. When you\'re asking yourself ""Does that make sense?"" constantly, it often means you\'re looking for someone else to confirm your thoughts feel valid. I\'m curious—can you think of a time when you expressed something without checking in first? What was that like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t really remember. A few times I spoke what was in my mind and it appeared I was talking rubbish to everyone. Sometimes it feels like I need permission to feel okay, as if happiness has to be justified. Why can\'t I be happy with the thing I say? I am not bullying anyone, I speak my mind'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Amy, it sounds like you\'re carrying this weight of needing external approval before you can accept your own thoughts. I wonder if you\'ve ever tried saying to yourself what you\'d say to a friend who was struggling with self-doubt? What would that look like?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m really trying to believe that I deserve rest — not just when I’ve earned it, but because I’m human. Kinda this? Sometimes I feel this way but its so much stress that in reality it seems there\'s no proof of that '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important distinction, Amy - knowing versus feeling. It\'s completely normal for our feelings to lag behind what we know is true. I\'m wondering if we could explore together what happens when you notice that gap between ""I know I deserve rest"" and ""I don\'t feel like I deserve it"" - what does that tension feel like in your body?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I cannot be present, I cannot sleep efficiently...I apologize all the time now… even for existing, it seems. I want to stop doing that'}]","I cannot be present, I cannot sleep efficiently...I apologize all the time now… even for existing, it seems. I want to stop doing that",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes so much sense, Amy. When we feel truly seen and understood, it can be incredibly grounding. I\'m wondering - what\'s one situation where you\'ve felt especially validated lately? Sometimes noticing those moments can help us understand what we need more of.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Amy. When you\'re asking yourself ""Does that make sense?"" constantly, it often means you\'re looking for someone else to confirm your thoughts feel valid. I\'m curious—can you think of a time when you expressed something without checking in first? What was that like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t really remember. A few times I spoke what was in my mind and it appeared I was talking rubbish to everyone. Sometimes it feels like I need permission to feel okay, as if happiness has to be justified. Why can\'t I be happy with the thing I say? I am not bullying anyone, I speak my mind'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Amy, it sounds like you\'re carrying this weight of needing external approval before you can accept your own thoughts. I wonder if you\'ve ever tried saying to yourself what you\'d say to a friend who was struggling with self-doubt? What would that look like?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m really trying to believe that I deserve rest — not just when I’ve earned it, but because I’m human. Kinda this? Sometimes I feel this way but its so much stress that in reality it seems there\'s no proof of that '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important distinction, Amy - knowing versus feeling. It\'s completely normal for our feelings to lag behind what we know is true. I\'m wondering if we could explore together what happens when you notice that gap between ""I know I deserve rest"" and ""I don\'t feel like I deserve it"" - what does that tension feel like in your body?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I cannot be present, I cannot sleep efficiently...I apologize all the time now… even for existing, it seems. I want to stop doing that'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It takes real courage to recognize when we\'re being kinder to others than ourselves, Amy. I want to gently challenge the idea that you need to apologize for existing - your worth isn\'t conditional on your ability to be ""present"" or ""efficient."" What if we explored what it might feel like to stop apologizing, even just for a moment?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Confidence used to come naturally, but now it feels so far away. I want to find my way back to it'}]","Confidence used to come naturally, but now it feels so far away. I want to find my way back to it",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
