"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Amy, thank you for reaching out. It means a lot that you took the time to say hello, especially when low mood can make even small interactions feel challenging. How have you been feeling since we last connected? I\'m here to listen and work with you on building those confidence-boosting habits we discussed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thank you. It’s strange. I know exactly what to say to help others, but when it comes to myself, I feel completely lost'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really common, Amy. It\'s like we often have a clear map for others but get confused about our own path sometimes. When you\'re feeling ""completely lost"" about yourself, what\'s the first thought that comes to mind? I\'m curious what\'s going through your head in those moments.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes. When you validate what I’m feeling, it’s like I can finally breathe. Validation feels like oxygen to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes so much sense, Amy. When we feel truly seen and understood, it can be incredibly grounding. I\'m wondering - what\'s one situation where you\'ve felt especially validated lately? Sometimes noticing those moments can help us understand what we need more of.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing, I guess. I catch myself always asking, ‘Does that make sense?’ — like I’m checking if I have the right to express things.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Amy. When you\'re asking yourself ""Does that make sense?"" constantly, it often means you\'re looking for someone else to confirm your thoughts feel valid. I\'m curious—can you think of a time when you expressed something without checking in first? What was that like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t really remember. A few times I spoke what was in my mind and it appeared I was talking rubbish to everyone. Sometimes it feels like I need permission to feel okay, as if happiness has to be justified. Why can\'t I be happy with the thing I say? I am not bullying anyone, I speak my mind'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Amy, it sounds like you\'re carrying this weight of needing external approval before you can accept your own thoughts. I wonder if you\'ve ever tried saying to yourself what you\'d say to a friend who was struggling with self-doubt? What would that look like?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m really trying to believe that I deserve rest — not just when I’ve earned it, but because I’m human. Kinda this? Sometimes I feel this way but its so much stress that in reality it seems there\'s no proof of that '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important distinction, Amy - knowing versus feeling. It\'s completely normal for our feelings to lag behind what we know is true. I\'m wondering if we could explore together what happens when you notice that gap between ""I know I deserve rest"" and ""I don\'t feel like I deserve it"" - what does that tension feel like in your body?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I cannot be present, I cannot sleep efficiently...I apologize all the time now… even for existing, it seems. I want to stop doing that'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It takes real courage to recognize when we\'re being kinder to others than ourselves, Amy. I want to gently challenge the idea that you need to apologize for existing - your worth isn\'t conditional on your ability to be ""present"" or ""efficient."" What if we explored what it might feel like to stop apologizing, even just for a moment?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Confidence used to come naturally, but now it feels so far away. I want to find my way back to it'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m really moved by how clearly you\'re describing this shift, Amy. When confidence used to feel ""natural,"" what was one small thing you remember doing that made you feel capable? I\'m curious what that looked like in your daily life.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve never thought about that. Thank you. I keep reminding myself that I don’t need to earn kindness — from others or from myself'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful realization, Amy. When you\'re extending this same understanding to how you treat others, I wonder if you\'ve noticed yourself speaking with more authenticity in conversations lately? What\'s one interaction where you felt this new self-kindness showing through?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Since my adolescence, I used to be the useful arm of my parents, to my siblings. I’m realizing that my self-worth can’t only come from being needed. It has to come from just being'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such an important shift in perspective, Amy. It takes real courage to untangle your worth from being needed. I wonder if there are any small moments lately where you\'ve noticed yourself treating yourself differently because you\'re recognizing your worth exists regardless of your role?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately I’ve been practicing seeing myself with softer eyes — less judgment, more understanding'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s beautiful, Amy. I\'m curious - when you\'re practicing those ""softer eyes,"" what does your body feel like? Sometimes these internal shifts show up most clearly in how we carry ourselves.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel more relaxed but not in the way I would want it to be. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m wondering what kind of relaxation would feel more aligned with what you\'re hoping for, Amy? Sometimes when we\'re used to being the ""useful arm,"" the idea of truly relaxing can feel unfamiliar or even a little unsettling. What would that ideal relaxation look like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Having time for myself not feeling guilty, on the beach or in a garden and fall asleep securely'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a beautiful picture, Amy. I\'m curious—what\'s one thing that might make it feel harder to let yourself fall asleep like that right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel kinda emotionless, apathetic maybe'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really important to notice, Amy. When we\'re working on self-worth, sometimes numbness can be our mind\'s way of protecting us from disappointment - like it\'s saying ""if I don\'t feel anything, I can\'t get hurt."" What\'s one small thing you might do today that wouldn\'t require you to feel anything special? Sometimes that tiny step can help us reconnect with ourselves.'}, {'role': user, 'content': be with my children and pass some time with them}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It takes real courage to notice this distance, Amy. When you\'re with your children, what\'s one thing that stands out to you right now - whether it\'s how you feel, what you\'re thinking, or what you\'re avoiding noticing?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'like, ""Am I being the present mother they need to have?""'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a human thing to wonder, Amy. I\'m curious - what would it feel like to be the ""present mother"" you imagine, versus being the one who\'s simply here with them right now? Sometimes the gap between our expectations and reality can feel so big.'}, {'role': user, 'content': How can I be just another person next to them?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful question, Amy. I\'m wondering—what does it feel like to imagine being ""just another person"" with your children? Is it about letting go of expectations, or finding a different kind of connection?'}, {'role': user, 'content': expectations I guess}]",expectations I guess,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
