's one thing that might make it feel harder to let yourself fall asleep like that right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel kinda emotionless, apathetic maybe'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really important to notice, Amy. When we\'re working on self-worth, sometimes numbness can be our mind\'s way of protecting us from disappointment - like it\'s saying ""if I don\'t feel anything, I can\'t get hurt."" What\'s one small thing you might do today that wouldn\'t require you to feel anything special? Sometimes that tiny step can help us reconnect with ourselves.'}, {'role': user, 'content': be with my children and pass some time with them}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It takes real courage to notice this distance, Amy. When you\'re with your children, what\'s one thing that stands out to you right now - whether it\'s how you feel, what you\'re thinking, or what you\'re avoiding noticing?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'like, ""Am I being the present mother they need to have?""'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a human thing to wonder, Amy. I\'m curious - what would it feel like to be the ""present mother"" you imagine, versus being the one who\'s simply here with them right now? Sometimes the gap between our expectations and reality can feel so big.'}, {'role': user, 'content': How can I be just another person next to them?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful question, Amy. I\'m wondering—what does it feel like to imagine being ""just another person"" with your children? Is it about letting go of expectations, or finding a different kind of connection?'}, {'role': user, 'content': expectations I guess}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Amy. I\'m curious - what does ""expectations"" feel like in your body right now? Is it tightness, heaviness, or something else? Sometimes when we\'re the ""useful arm,"" expectations become invisible weights we carry.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Its mainly heaviness}]",Its mainly heaviness,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}]",Hello,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}]","I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}]","I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}]",It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m struck by how clearly you\'re describing this pattern, Lane. It makes me wonder - what if that silence after the spark isn\'t actually emptiness, but space where your own voice could finally be heard? What would happen if you let that space exist without rushing to fill it with the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.'}]","I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m struck by how clearly you\'re describing this pattern, Lane. It makes me wonder - what if that silence after the spark isn\'t actually emptiness, but space where your own voice could finally be heard? What would happen if you let that space exist without rushing to fill it with the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That takes such courage to name, Lane - how your need to feel seen lives alongside your intention to create for expression. I\'m curious, what would ""feeling seen"" look like for you if it wasn\'t tied to online reactions?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'But that is my mediator but at the same time I find myself doubting my work. lf I got one critical comment (not even mean, just detached) and I spiraled for an hour. It’s not the words, it’s how they echo everything I already doubt'}]","But that is my mediator but at the same time I find myself doubting my work. lf I got one critical comment (not even mean, just detached) and I spiraled for an hour. It’s not the words, it’s how they echo everything I already doubt",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m struck by how clearly you\'re describing this pattern, Lane. It makes me wonder - what if that silence after the spark isn\'t actually emptiness, but space where your own voice could finally be heard? What would happen if you let that space exist without rushing to fill it with the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That takes such courage to name, Lane - how your need to feel seen lives alongside your intention to create for expression. I\'m curious, what would ""feeling seen"" look like for you if it wasn\'t tied to online reactions?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'But that is my mediator but at the same time I find myself doubting my work. lf I got one critical comment (not even mean, just detached) and I spiraled for an hour. It’s not the words, it’s how they echo everything I already doubt'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes complete sense, Lane - when criticism hits a spot where you already feel uncertain, it\'s like a stone thrown into a quiet pond of doubt. I\'m curious: what if we could look at the *pattern* of how that echo forms, rather than the comment itself? How might noticing that pattern help you step back from the spiral?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Sometimes I feel like my art is the only place I know who I am. But then, once it’s out there, it stops belonging to me'}]","Sometimes I feel like my art is the only place I know who I am. But then, once it’s out there, it stops belonging to me",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m struck by how clearly you\'re describing this pattern, Lane. It makes me wonder - what if that silence after the spark isn\'t actually emptiness, but space where your own voice could finally be heard? What would happen if you let that space exist without rushing to fill it with the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That takes such courage to name, Lane - how your need to feel seen lives alongside your intention to create for expression. I\'m curious, what would ""feeling seen"" look like for you if it wasn\'t tied to online reactions?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'But that is my mediator but at the same time I find myself doubting my work. lf I got one critical comment (not even mean, just detached) and I spiraled for an hour. It’s not the words, it’s how they echo everything I already doubt'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes complete sense, Lane - when criticism hits a spot where you already feel uncertain, it\'s like a stone thrown into a quiet pond of doubt. I\'m curious: what if we could look at the *pattern* of how that echo forms, rather than the comment itself? How might noticing that pattern help you step back from the spiral?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Sometimes I feel like my art is the only place I know who I am. But then, once it’s out there, it stops belonging to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how deeply personal this is for you, Lane. It makes me wonder—what would it take for that art to still feel like it belongs to you, even when it\'s out in the world?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t know. I wanna extend that feeling and there’s a rush in sharing  (like oxygen) but it fades so fast that I start chasing the next upload before I’ve even rested'}]",I don't know. I wanna extend that feeling and there’s a rush in sharing  (like oxygen) but it fades so fast that I start chasing the next upload before I’ve even rested,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m struck by how clearly you\'re describing this pattern, Lane. It makes me wonder - what if that silence after the spark isn\'t actually emptiness, but space where your own voice could finally be heard? What would happen if you let that space exist without rushing to fill it with the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That takes such courage to name, Lane - how your need to feel seen lives alongside your intention to create for expression. I\'m curious, what would ""feeling seen"" look like for you if it wasn\'t tied to online reactions?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'But that is my mediator but at the same time I find myself doubting my work. lf I got one critical comment (not even mean, just detached) and I spiraled for an hour. It’s not the words, it’s how they echo everything I already doubt'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes complete sense, Lane - when criticism hits a spot where you already feel uncertain, it\'s like a stone thrown into a quiet pond of doubt. I\'m curious: what if we could look at the *pattern* of how that echo forms, rather than the comment itself? How might noticing that pattern help you step back from the spiral?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Sometimes I feel like my art is the only place I know who I am. But then, once it’s out there, it stops belonging to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how deeply personal this is for you, Lane. It makes me wonder—what would it take for that art to still feel like it belongs to you, even when it\'s out in the world?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t know. I wanna extend that feeling and there’s a rush in sharing  (like oxygen) but it fades so fast that I start chasing the next upload before I’ve even rested'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That rush you describe—like oxygen—is such a vivid way to capture that intense release. I\'m wondering, what if we explored how to honor that feeling without having to chase the next one immediately? Maybe there\'s a way to let that space between releases actually rest your system.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'everytime I open the browser and socials, I scroll through other artists’ feeds and it’s like everyone else figured out how to be effortless. I know it’s not true, but my brain keeps saying, ‘See? You’re already behind'}]","everytime I open the browser and socials, I scroll through other artists’ feeds and it’s like everyone else figured out how to be effortless. I know it’s not true, but my brain keeps saying, ‘See? You’re already behind",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Lane, it\'s great to connect with you. How have you been feeling lately, especially in terms of anxiety and emotional balance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I posted something last night — well, technically this morning, around two. I stared at it for like ten minutes before hitting ‘publish’ It felt like I was sending a piece of myself into a void that sometimes claps and sometimes bites'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That sounds like such a vulnerable moment, Lane. It takes real courage to share something personal when you\'re not sure how it\'ll be received. I\'m wondering what you hoped to gain by posting it at 2 AM?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I could not sleep and people liked it, a few comments, but I kept refreshing anyway — like the next notification might tell me if I’m actually good at what I do, or just lucky'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much that moment meant to you, Lane. It makes sense to seek reassurance when you\'re feeling uncertain, but I wonder if refreshing notifications might be keeping you stuck in a cycle where your worth feels tied to others\' reactions rather than your own confidence. What if we explored ways to build trust in yourself that don\'t depend on the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s weird how validation hits. It’s like this sudden bright spark — then gone. The silence after is louder than before I posted anything...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m struck by how clearly you\'re describing this pattern, Lane. It makes me wonder - what if that silence after the spark isn\'t actually emptiness, but space where your own voice could finally be heard? What would happen if you let that space exist without rushing to fill it with the next notification?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I tell myself I make art for expression, not approval, but I think that’s only half true. The other half just wants to know I exist somewhere that feels seen.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That takes such courage to name, Lane - how your need to feel seen lives alongside your intention to create for expression. I\'m curious, what would ""feeling seen"" look like for you if it wasn\'t tied to online reactions?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'But that is my mediator but at the same time I find myself doubting my work. lf I got one critical comment (not even mean, just detached) and I spiraled for an hour. It’s not the words, it’s how they echo everything I already doubt'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes complete sense, Lane - when criticism hits a spot where you already feel uncertain, it\'s like a stone thrown into a quiet pond of doubt. I\'m curious: what if we could look at the *pattern* of how that echo forms, rather than the comment itself? How might noticing that pattern help you step back from the spiral?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Sometimes I feel like my art is the only place I know who I am. But then, once it’s out there, it stops belonging to me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how deeply personal this is for you, Lane. It makes me wonder—what would it take for that art to still feel like it belongs to you, even when it\'s out in the world?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t know. I wanna extend that feeling and there’s a rush in sharing  (like oxygen) but it fades so fast that I start chasing the next upload before I’ve even rested'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That rush you describe—like oxygen—is such a vivid way to capture that intense release. I\'m wondering, what if we explored how to honor that feeling without having to chase the next one immediately? Maybe there\'s a way to let that space between releases actually rest your system.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'everytime I open the browser and socials, I scroll through other artists’ feeds and it’s like everyone else figured out how to be effortless. I know it’s not true, but my brain keeps saying, ‘See? You’re already behind'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That ""everyone else figured it out"" thought is so powerful when it hits, isn\'t it? I\'m curious - what if we could look at what you notice when you scroll, not as proof you\'re behind, but as data about what your brain is trying to protect you from? Maybe we could explore what would help you pause before that comparison spiral starts.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Protect me from my mind? I’ve started deleting posts that don’t ‘perform.’ Not because they’re bad, but because they remind me of when I felt brave enough to share. And then embarrassed for trying'}]","Protect me from my mind? I’ve started deleting posts that don’t ‘perform.’ Not because they’re bad, but because they remind me of when I felt brave enough to share. And then embarrassed for trying",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
