isn’t falling apart. At this point, I don’t think I can help anyone, everything I say feels hollow.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a heavy thought, Ruth. When you\'re this tired, even your own kindness can feel out of reach. But remember - you\'re not failing them when you\'re struggling. You\'re showing them what it means to be human, and that\'s actually teaching them something much more important than perfection ever could be.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Maybe I’m just playing the role of a professional, hiding how bad things really are'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes sense you\'d feel this way when you\'re carrying so much - it\'s exhausting to feel like you\'re performing a role while your own emotions are running high. But your work as a social worker isn\'t just a performance; it\'s an expression of your deep care for others, even when you\'re struggling. Would it help to talk about what specifically makes you feel like you\'re ""hiding"" who you really are right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Maybe I need to step back from work for a while, at least until I can sort myself out. I don’t know how I can help other people when I’m in this state. It makes me feel like such a fraud.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it\'s completely understandable to feel this way when you\'re this exhausted. But here\'s what I wonder: when you\'re working with clients who feel like frauds, what do you tell them about how being human means sometimes feeling imperfect? Your worth isn\'t measured by how much you can do right now - it\'s measured by how deeply you care, even when you\'re struggling.'}, {'role': user, 'content': You can’t be sure that’s true. I’m not even sure myself!}]",You can’t be sure that’s true. I’m not even sure myself!,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
