"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}]",I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}]",It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}]","My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}]","I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how hard it is to hold both anger toward your wife and toward yourself simultaneously. When you feel this self-directed anger, what does it say to you about what you\'re hoping for or expecting from yourself in these situations?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.'}]","Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how hard it is to hold both anger toward your wife and toward yourself simultaneously. When you feel this self-directed anger, what does it say to you about what you\'re hoping for or expecting from yourself in these situations?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how carefully you\'re trying to protect your children while also honoring your own emotional needs. When you walk away, does that help you feel more in control, or does it sometimes leave you feeling disconnected afterward?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Of course I feel disconnected. I’m not really present. I just leave my wife to deal with it all on her own. It’s just too much.}]",Of course I feel disconnected. I’m not really present. I just leave my wife to deal with it all on her own. It’s just too much.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how hard it is to hold both anger toward your wife and toward yourself simultaneously. When you feel this self-directed anger, what does it say to you about what you\'re hoping for or expecting from yourself in these situations?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how carefully you\'re trying to protect your children while also honoring your own emotional needs. When you walk away, does that help you feel more in control, or does it sometimes leave you feeling disconnected afterward?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Of course I feel disconnected. I’m not really present. I just leave my wife to deal with it all on her own. It’s just too much.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m hearing how much you\'re trying to protect both your family and yourself, even if it means stepping back. When you leave, does your children\'s learning situation ever feel like it\'s improving, or does it sometimes feel like they\'re missing out on important moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m disappointed by this behavior that led to all the problems at school. I’ve tried to explain rationally why it’s wrong, but it only turns into more arguments.'}]","I’m disappointed by this behavior that led to all the problems at school. I’ve tried to explain rationally why it’s wrong, but it only turns into more arguments.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how hard it is to hold both anger toward your wife and toward yourself simultaneously. When you feel this self-directed anger, what does it say to you about what you\'re hoping for or expecting from yourself in these situations?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how carefully you\'re trying to protect your children while also honoring your own emotional needs. When you walk away, does that help you feel more in control, or does it sometimes leave you feeling disconnected afterward?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Of course I feel disconnected. I’m not really present. I just leave my wife to deal with it all on her own. It’s just too much.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m hearing how much you\'re trying to protect both your family and yourself, even if it means stepping back. When you leave, does your children\'s learning situation ever feel like it\'s improving, or does it sometimes feel like they\'re missing out on important moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m disappointed by this behavior that led to all the problems at school. I’ve tried to explain rationally why it’s wrong, but it only turns into more arguments.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how thoughtful it is that you\'re trying to approach this with reason, even when it doesn\'t seem to be landing. When you see your children acting out, what emotions do you notice in them that might be driving these arguments, even if you\'re focusing on the logic?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'They’re angry. I don’t even know about what. And I’ve told them, when you’re angry, you need to walk away until you calm down.'}]","They’re angry. I don’t even know about what. And I’ve told them, when you’re angry, you need to walk away until you calm down.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how hard it is to hold both anger toward your wife and toward yourself simultaneously. When you feel this self-directed anger, what does it say to you about what you\'re hoping for or expecting from yourself in these situations?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how carefully you\'re trying to protect your children while also honoring your own emotional needs. When you walk away, does that help you feel more in control, or does it sometimes leave you feeling disconnected afterward?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Of course I feel disconnected. I’m not really present. I just leave my wife to deal with it all on her own. It’s just too much.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m hearing how much you\'re trying to protect both your family and yourself, even if it means stepping back. When you leave, does your children\'s learning situation ever feel like it\'s improving, or does it sometimes feel like they\'re missing out on important moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m disappointed by this behavior that led to all the problems at school. I’ve tried to explain rationally why it’s wrong, but it only turns into more arguments.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how thoughtful it is that you\'re trying to approach this with reason, even when it doesn\'t seem to be landing. When you see your children acting out, what emotions do you notice in them that might be driving these arguments, even if you\'re focusing on the logic?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'They’re angry. I don’t even know about what. And I’ve told them, when you’re angry, you need to walk away until you calm down.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much you care about your children\'s emotional growth. When you\'re hoping they feel calm or responsible, what might they actually be feeling or needing in those moments that you haven\'t considered yet?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Family is all you have, and if someone is struggling with something, they should just come out and say it.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much you value open communication in your family. It\'s interesting how you\'re teaching your children to express themselves while also noticing how you sometimes step away when things get tough - what do you think might be happening in those moments when you walk away?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'As I\'ve told you, when you get angry, you need to walk away until you calm down. '}]","As I've told you, when you get angry, you need to walk away until you calm down. ",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Aaron, thanks for reaching out. I\'m here with you. How have you been feeling lately?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I’m having problems with one of my children. The school has complained about fights with other kids and talking back to teachers.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m really glad you\'re sharing this with me. School challenges with children can be so stressful - how has this been affecting you emotionally and in your family communication?'}, {'role': user, 'content': It’s just another thing that’s going wrong in my life right now. Things aren’t the way they used to be.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming that can feel when it seems like everything\'s shifting. When you say things aren\'t the way they used to be, what specific emotions come up for you in those moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My wife keeps coddling our children when there should be consequences. Otherwise, how will they ever learn? I’ve tried talking to her calmly about it, but nothing has changed.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Aaron, I\'m hearing how much you care about your children\'s growth and how frustrated you feel when you can\'t see the changes you want. When you think about these conversations with your wife, what\'s the most difficult emotion you\'re holding onto?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m angry, not just at her, but at myself as well.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how hard it is to hold both anger toward your wife and toward yourself simultaneously. When you feel this self-directed anger, what does it say to you about what you\'re hoping for or expecting from yourself in these situations?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Lately, I can’t help but get very angry because nobody seems to listen to me or take me seriously. But I don’t like yelling at my children, that’s not how they learn. So I just walk away.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how carefully you\'re trying to protect your children while also honoring your own emotional needs. When you walk away, does that help you feel more in control, or does it sometimes leave you feeling disconnected afterward?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Of course I feel disconnected. I’m not really present. I just leave my wife to deal with it all on her own. It’s just too much.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m hearing how much you\'re trying to protect both your family and yourself, even if it means stepping back. When you leave, does your children\'s learning situation ever feel like it\'s improving, or does it sometimes feel like they\'re missing out on important moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’m disappointed by this behavior that led to all the problems at school. I’ve tried to explain rationally why it’s wrong, but it only turns into more arguments.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I notice how thoughtful it is that you\'re trying to approach this with reason, even when it doesn\'t seem to be landing. When you see your children acting out, what emotions do you notice in them that might be driving these arguments, even if you\'re focusing on the logic?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'They’re angry. I don’t even know about what. And I’ve told them, when you’re angry, you need to walk away until you calm down.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much you care about your children\'s emotional growth. When you\'re hoping they feel calm or responsible, what might they actually be feeling or needing in those moments that you haven\'t considered yet?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Family is all you have, and if someone is struggling with something, they should just come out and say it.'}]","Family is all you have, and if someone is struggling with something, they should just come out and say it.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}]","I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}]","I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}]","It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much weight these responsibilities carry, and how much you\'re hoping others will see your strength. What would you say to yourself if you weren\'t holding all that weight and no one was watching?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.'}]","Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much weight these responsibilities carry, and how much you\'re hoping others will see your strength. What would you say to yourself if you weren\'t holding all that weight and no one was watching?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It sounds like you\'re carrying so much responsibility that it\'s hard to see yourself as capable. When you think about being a good parent, what does that look like to you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being a good parent means loving my kids, of course. But I’m starting to see that love isn’t enough when I’m running on empty. If I’m not okay, I can’t really be there for them the way they need.'}]","Being a good parent means loving my kids, of course. But I’m starting to see that love isn’t enough when I’m running on empty. If I’m not okay, I can’t really be there for them the way they need.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}]",hello!,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much weight these responsibilities carry, and how much you\'re hoping others will see your strength. What would you say to yourself if you weren\'t holding all that weight and no one was watching?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It sounds like you\'re carrying so much responsibility that it\'s hard to see yourself as capable. When you think about being a good parent, what does that look like to you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being a good parent means loving my kids, of course. But I’m starting to see that love isn’t enough when I’m running on empty. If I’m not okay, I can’t really be there for them the way they need.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful realization, Ruth. What if we reframe it: when you\'re able to care for yourself, you\'re actually giving your kids the gift of seeing what healthy self-care looks like.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, that’s true. I just don’t really know what I’m missing when it comes to taking care of myself. '}]","Yes, that’s true. I just don’t really know what I’m missing when it comes to taking care of myself. ",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much weight these responsibilities carry, and how much you\'re hoping others will see your strength. What would you say to yourself if you weren\'t holding all that weight and no one was watching?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It sounds like you\'re carrying so much responsibility that it\'s hard to see yourself as capable. When you think about being a good parent, what does that look like to you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being a good parent means loving my kids, of course. But I’m starting to see that love isn’t enough when I’m running on empty. If I’m not okay, I can’t really be there for them the way they need.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful realization, Ruth. What if we reframe it: when you\'re able to care for yourself, you\'re actually giving your kids the gift of seeing what healthy self-care looks like.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, that’s true. I just don’t really know what I’m missing when it comes to taking care of myself. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, that\'s such a thoughtful question. What if we start by noticing just one small moment each day where you could pause and check in with yourself—like when you\'re sipping your morning coffee or before you start your next task. What would that moment feel like if you allowed yourself to be fully present?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don’t know if I could really focus on myself like that. It sounds simple, but in my day-to-day life it feels almost impossible, even something as small as a coffee break gets swallowed by everything else. The reality is just… a lot'}]","I don’t know if I could really focus on myself like that. It sounds simple, but in my day-to-day life it feels almost impossible, even something as small as a coffee break gets swallowed by everything else. The reality is just… a lot",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much weight these responsibilities carry, and how much you\'re hoping others will see your strength. What would you say to yourself if you weren\'t holding all that weight and no one was watching?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It sounds like you\'re carrying so much responsibility that it\'s hard to see yourself as capable. When you think about being a good parent, what does that look like to you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being a good parent means loving my kids, of course. But I’m starting to see that love isn’t enough when I’m running on empty. If I’m not okay, I can’t really be there for them the way they need.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful realization, Ruth. What if we reframe it: when you\'re able to care for yourself, you\'re actually giving your kids the gift of seeing what healthy self-care looks like.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, that’s true. I just don’t really know what I’m missing when it comes to taking care of myself. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, that\'s such a thoughtful question. What if we start by noticing just one small moment each day where you could pause and check in with yourself—like when you\'re sipping your morning coffee or before you start your next task. What would that moment feel like if you allowed yourself to be fully present?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don’t know if I could really focus on myself like that. It sounds simple, but in my day-to-day life it feels almost impossible, even something as small as a coffee break gets swallowed by everything else. The reality is just… a lot'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how much everything weighs on you. What if we imagine pausing for just 30 seconds to notice one small sensation—like the warmth of your coffee cup in your hands—instead of thinking about everything else?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It feels like you’re suggesting exercises I just don’t have the time or focus to follow through with. I’d love to understand the idea, but honestly, I don’t believe I’m capable of adding yet another routine to the thousand I already have.'}]","It feels like you’re suggesting exercises I just don’t have the time or focus to follow through with. I’d love to understand the idea, but honestly, I don’t believe I’m capable of adding yet another routine to the thousand I already have.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': hello!}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Ruth! I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today? What\'s on your mind?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I feel like I’m always checking if what I say sounds okay. Even at work.  I’ll reread an email three times before sending it, just in case it comes off wrong. It’s exhausting, but I can’t seem to switch it off. Does that make sense?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, it makes complete sense that this would feel exhausting. So many people get caught in these loops of self-checking when they\'re anxious about how others might perceive them. What emotion do you notice most when you\'re in that moment—like fear, worry, or something else?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I catch myself asking people if what I said makes sense, even when I already know it does.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how draining it must be to constantly seek reassurance. What emotion do you notice most when you catch yourself asking if what you said makes sense?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s important to me that others recognise I’m capable. But sometimes the weight of everything: work, the kids, all the little responsibilities just feels like too much to hold together.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how much weight these responsibilities carry, and how much you\'re hoping others will see your strength. What would you say to yourself if you weren\'t holding all that weight and no one was watching?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ouch… if things ever got to that point, I’d be really worried about my kids. I can’t fail them — but sometimes I’m scared that, without meaning to, I might be hurting their lives anyway.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It sounds like you\'re carrying so much responsibility that it\'s hard to see yourself as capable. When you think about being a good parent, what does that look like to you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being a good parent means loving my kids, of course. But I’m starting to see that love isn’t enough when I’m running on empty. If I’m not okay, I can’t really be there for them the way they need.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a meaningful realization, Ruth. What if we reframe it: when you\'re able to care for yourself, you\'re actually giving your kids the gift of seeing what healthy self-care looks like.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yes, that’s true. I just don’t really know what I’m missing when it comes to taking care of myself. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Ruth, that\'s such a thoughtful question. What if we start by noticing just one small moment each day where you could pause and check in with yourself—like when you\'re sipping your morning coffee or before you start your next task. What would that moment feel like if you allowed yourself to be fully present?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don’t know if I could really focus on myself like that. It sounds simple, but in my day-to-day life it feels almost impossible, even something as small as a coffee break gets swallowed by everything else. The reality is just… a lot'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': I hear how much everything weighs on you. What if we imagine pausing for just 30 seconds to notice one small sensation—like the warmth of your coffee cup in your hands—instead of thinking about everything else?}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It feels like you’re suggesting exercises I just don’t have the time or focus to follow through with. I’d love to understand the idea, but honestly, I don’t believe I’m capable of adding yet another routine to the thousand I already have.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how overwhelming it feels to think about adding anything new when you\'re already stretched so thin. What if we reframe it: instead of adding a new routine, we could look for tiny moments where you\'re already doing something gentle for yourself—like taking a breath before a meeting or letting yourself pause for a few seconds while making coffee. How would that feel if we treated those as natural pauses rather than extra tasks?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t know... May be I can ask some of my colleagues how the manage their own stress? Does that make sense?'}]",I don't know... May be I can ask some of my colleagues how the manage their own stress? Does that make sense?,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
