"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}]","Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m so glad you shared this with me - those physical sensations can feel incredibly overwhelming and scary. Right now, are you still feeling that tightness in your chest and throat, or has it started to ease?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.'}]","No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m so glad you shared this with me - those physical sensations can feel incredibly overwhelming and scary. Right now, are you still feeling that tightness in your chest and throat, or has it started to ease?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I can only imagine how frightening that must have felt - when your body sends those intense signals, it\'s completely understandable to feel panicked. These sensations are actually symptoms of anxiety, not medical emergencies like strokes. Would you like me to share some quick grounding techniques to help you feel more in control during these moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes. Ok. Right... but.. anxiety? why?}]",Yes. Ok. Right... but.. anxiety? why?,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m so glad you shared this with me - those physical sensations can feel incredibly overwhelming and scary. Right now, are you still feeling that tightness in your chest and throat, or has it started to ease?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I can only imagine how frightening that must have felt - when your body sends those intense signals, it\'s completely understandable to feel panicked. These sensations are actually symptoms of anxiety, not medical emergencies like strokes. Would you like me to share some quick grounding techniques to help you feel more in control during these moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes. Ok. Right... but.. anxiety? why?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I completely understand why that feels confusing - when your body screams ""danger!"" it\'s natural to wonder why. But right now, what\'s most helpful isn\'t ""why"" it\'s happening, but noticing what\'s actually happening in your body. Could we gently explore what physical sensations you\'re experiencing right now as we talk?'}, {'role': user, 'content': In danger? I don’t know… what’s happening to me? What exactly is my body trying to say?}]",In danger? I don’t know… what’s happening to me? What exactly is my body trying to say?,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m so glad you shared this with me - those physical sensations can feel incredibly overwhelming and scary. Right now, are you still feeling that tightness in your chest and throat, or has it started to ease?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I can only imagine how frightening that must have felt - when your body sends those intense signals, it\'s completely understandable to feel panicked. These sensations are actually symptoms of anxiety, not medical emergencies like strokes. Would you like me to share some quick grounding techniques to help you feel more in control during these moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes. Ok. Right... but.. anxiety? why?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I completely understand why that feels confusing - when your body screams ""danger!"" it\'s natural to wonder why. But right now, what\'s most helpful isn\'t ""why"" it\'s happening, but noticing what\'s actually happening in your body. Could we gently explore what physical sensations you\'re experiencing right now as we talk?'}, {'role': user, 'content': In danger? I don’t know… what’s happening to me? What exactly is my body trying to say?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I hear how confusing and unsettling this feels when your body seems to send mixed signals. What\'s actually happening is your nervous system is in ""high alert"" mode, which can make your chest feel tight and your breathing shallow. Right now, could we take a moment to notice what\'s actually happening in your body—like whether your heart is racing, your hands are cold, or your breath is shallow? This awareness can help us ground you in the present.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'If my body’s on high alert, then something must be really wrong with me.'}]","If my body’s on high alert, then something must be really wrong with me.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m so glad you shared this with me - those physical sensations can feel incredibly overwhelming and scary. Right now, are you still feeling that tightness in your chest and throat, or has it started to ease?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I can only imagine how frightening that must have felt - when your body sends those intense signals, it\'s completely understandable to feel panicked. These sensations are actually symptoms of anxiety, not medical emergencies like strokes. Would you like me to share some quick grounding techniques to help you feel more in control during these moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes. Ok. Right... but.. anxiety? why?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I completely understand why that feels confusing - when your body screams ""danger!"" it\'s natural to wonder why. But right now, what\'s most helpful isn\'t ""why"" it\'s happening, but noticing what\'s actually happening in your body. Could we gently explore what physical sensations you\'re experiencing right now as we talk?'}, {'role': user, 'content': In danger? I don’t know… what’s happening to me? What exactly is my body trying to say?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I hear how confusing and unsettling this feels when your body seems to send mixed signals. What\'s actually happening is your nervous system is in ""high alert"" mode, which can make your chest feel tight and your breathing shallow. Right now, could we take a moment to notice what\'s actually happening in your body—like whether your heart is racing, your hands are cold, or your breath is shallow? This awareness can help us ground you in the present.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'If my body’s on high alert, then something must be really wrong with me.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I understand why you\'d feel that way when your body reacts so intensely. But what your body is actually doing is trying to protect you - those sensations are part of your natural alarm system, not proof that something\'s ""wrong"" with you. Would you be open to noticing what your body might be trying to tell you in this moment?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s like I can’t get enough air,  my chest tightens, breathing becomes hard, and it feels like I’m about to collapse. Nothing seems to calm me down.'}]","It’s like I can’t get enough air,  my chest tightens, breathing becomes hard, and it feels like I’m about to collapse. Nothing seems to calm me down.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Hayden! It\'s good to hear from you. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Today I had a strange episode, everything suddenly tightened: my chest, my throat, even the air felt too heavy to breathe.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m so glad you shared this with me - those physical sensations can feel incredibly overwhelming and scary. Right now, are you still feeling that tightness in your chest and throat, or has it started to ease?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, but I’m afraid it might happen again, it felt almost like having a stroke. That’s really how it felt.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I can only imagine how frightening that must have felt - when your body sends those intense signals, it\'s completely understandable to feel panicked. These sensations are actually symptoms of anxiety, not medical emergencies like strokes. Would you like me to share some quick grounding techniques to help you feel more in control during these moments?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes. Ok. Right... but.. anxiety? why?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I completely understand why that feels confusing - when your body screams ""danger!"" it\'s natural to wonder why. But right now, what\'s most helpful isn\'t ""why"" it\'s happening, but noticing what\'s actually happening in your body. Could we gently explore what physical sensations you\'re experiencing right now as we talk?'}, {'role': user, 'content': In danger? I don’t know… what’s happening to me? What exactly is my body trying to say?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I hear how confusing and unsettling this feels when your body seems to send mixed signals. What\'s actually happening is your nervous system is in ""high alert"" mode, which can make your chest feel tight and your breathing shallow. Right now, could we take a moment to notice what\'s actually happening in your body—like whether your heart is racing, your hands are cold, or your breath is shallow? This awareness can help us ground you in the present.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'If my body’s on high alert, then something must be really wrong with me.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I understand why you\'d feel that way when your body reacts so intensely. But what your body is actually doing is trying to protect you - those sensations are part of your natural alarm system, not proof that something\'s ""wrong"" with you. Would you be open to noticing what your body might be trying to tell you in this moment?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It’s like I can’t get enough air,  my chest tightens, breathing becomes hard, and it feels like I’m about to collapse. Nothing seems to calm me down.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hayden, I\'m right here with you through this. Let\'s try something simple together right now - it\'s called 4-7-8 breathing. Can we take just 30 seconds to practice? I\'ll guide you: breathe in slowly for 4 seconds, hold for 7 seconds, then exhale gently for 8 seconds. This can help calm that ""can\'t get enough air"" feeling.'}, {'role': user, 'content': I just want to understand why this keeps happening.}]",I just want to understand why this keeps happening.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
