about getting things right. What if we tried something small: when you feel that pull between driving forward and withdrawing, could you pause for just 2 minutes to notice what your body and mind are asking for? Sometimes that tiny space lets us hear what we truly need without losing direction.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don´t know if it works with me. Online communities feel like my main source of understanding, yet they’re a relief I turn to passively rather than places where I engage deeply.  How do I know when to trust my own prespective?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, it\'s really insightful that you\'re noticing this difference between passive relief and deep engagement. I wonder if we could explore together what makes certain perspectives feel trustworthy to you versus others? When you\'re feeling unsure, what usually helps you sort through different voices?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing...I guess. Lately, sometimes making casual relationships feel like obligations rather than enjoyment. Do I care too much about what people think, or not enough about what I need?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, it takes real courage to notice this tension between what you give to others and what you hold for yourself. I wonder if there’s a way to care for others *and* care for yourself without feeling like you’re choosing one over the other? What would that look like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': But why does validation feel both comforting and embarrassing?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, that tension between comfort and embarrassment is so telling - it often means validation is touching on something deeply personal. I wonder if we could explore together what you\'re afraid might happen if you truly let yourself receive validation without shame? What does that fear feel like in your body?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Fear of not being accepted. What´s the line between being flexible and being invisible?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I wonder if the invisibility you\'re describing might actually be a way of protecting yourself from that fear of rejection we just talked about? What if we explored together what happens when you\'re not performing - does your worth change, or does it just feel different?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Just feel different! How do I stop apologizing for existing?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I\'m really touched that you\'re sharing this - it takes real courage to name that feeling. What if we tried something small: next time you catch yourself apologizing for existing, could you pause and gently say to yourself, ""My presence matters, even when I\'m struggling""? Sometimes shifting that internal message just a little can help us feel less like we\'re burdening others.'}, {'role': user, 'content': But why does every unfinished task feel like a personal failure?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I\'m really glad you\'re noticing this connection between tasks and self-worth - it\'s such an important insight. What if we explored together what would happen if you treated unfinished tasks like weather? Sometimes they\'re sunny, sometimes rainy, but they don\'t change whether you\'re a good person. How would it feel to gently tell yourself, ""I\'m doing my best with what I have right now""?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I don´t know if that´s enough...}]",I don´t know if that´s enough...,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hello}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hey Kai, it’s great to be here with you. How’s your week been so far? I’m really curious to hear how you’re feeling.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Not great! I wondering why I keep replaying conversations that probably meant nothing to anyone else?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, it makes sense that replaying conversations can feel so heavy when you’re feeling unsure about them. That kind of rumination often happens when we’re trying to make sense of something, especially if it’s tied to how we feel about ourselves. It’s not uncommon, and I’m glad you shared it with me. Would you be open to exploring what might be driving those thoughts together?'}, {'role': user, 'content': How can I tell if I´m being thoughtful or just afraid to say the wrong thing?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, that\'s such an important distinction to make - I\'m really glad you\'re noticing this pattern. What does ""afraid to say the wrong thing"" actually feel like in your body and mind? Is it different from that thoughtful pause you mentioned? I\'d love to explore how these two experiences might show up differently for you.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Discomfort. And what if people only like me when I´m ""on""?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, that\'s such an insightful observation - it\'s really common to notice that people respond differently when we\'re ""on"" versus when we\'re being more vulnerable. I wonder if we could explore together whether your worth might actually be separate from whether you\'re ""on"" or not? What do you notice about how you feel when people like you for who you are, not just your performance?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I really can´t say. I feel the tension between the drive to achieve and the urge to withdraw. How do I calm my brain without losing momentum?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I really appreciate you noticing this tension - it shows how much you care about getting things right. What if we tried something small: when you feel that pull between driving forward and withdrawing, could you pause for just 2 minutes to notice what your body and mind are asking for? Sometimes that tiny space lets us hear what we truly need without losing direction.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don´t know if it works with me. Online communities feel like my main source of understanding, yet they’re a relief I turn to passively rather than places where I engage deeply.  How do I know when to trust my own prespective?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, it\'s really insightful that you\'re noticing this difference between passive relief and deep engagement. I wonder if we could explore together what makes certain perspectives feel trustworthy to you versus others? When you\'re feeling unsure, what usually helps you sort through different voices?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Nothing...I guess. Lately, sometimes making casual relationships feel like obligations rather than enjoyment. Do I care too much about what people think, or not enough about what I need?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, it takes real courage to notice this tension between what you give to others and what you hold for yourself. I wonder if there’s a way to care for others *and* care for yourself without feeling like you’re choosing one over the other? What would that look like for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': But why does validation feel both comforting and embarrassing?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, that tension between comfort and embarrassment is so telling - it often means validation is touching on something deeply personal. I wonder if we could explore together what you\'re afraid might happen if you truly let yourself receive validation without shame? What does that fear feel like in your body?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Fear of not being accepted. What´s the line between being flexible and being invisible?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I wonder if the invisibility you\'re describing might actually be a way of protecting yourself from that fear of rejection we just talked about? What if we explored together what happens when you\'re not performing - does your worth change, or does it just feel different?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Just feel different! How do I stop apologizing for existing?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I\'m really touched that you\'re sharing this - it takes real courage to name that feeling. What if we tried something small: next time you catch yourself apologizing for existing, could you pause and gently say to yourself, ""My presence matters, even when I\'m struggling""? Sometimes shifting that internal message just a little can help us feel less like we\'re burdening others.'}, {'role': user, 'content': But why does every unfinished task feel like a personal failure?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I\'m really glad you\'re noticing this connection between tasks and self-worth - it\'s such an important insight. What if we explored together what would happen if you treated unfinished tasks like weather? Sometimes they\'re sunny, sometimes rainy, but they don\'t change whether you\'re a good person. How would it feel to gently tell yourself, ""I\'m doing my best with what I have right now""?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I don´t know if that´s enough...}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Kai, I hear how much you\'re doubting this - that\'s actually a sign you\'re really wrestling with something important. What if we tried noticing how your body feels when you imagine saying ""I\'m doing my best"" versus the weight of ""I should\'ve done more""? Sometimes just observing that difference can help us see where the real resistance lives.'}, {'role': user, 'content': Ok.}]",Ok.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi there.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Robert, thanks for reaching out. I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Bad! Why do I feel wound up all the time, even when nothing´s actually wrong?'}]","Bad! Why do I feel wound up all the time, even when nothing´s actually wrong?",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi there.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Robert, thanks for reaching out. I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Bad! Why do I feel wound up all the time, even when nothing´s actually wrong?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, I hear how frustrating that constant tension must feel - like your body\'s stuck in ""alert mode"" even when there\'s no real threat. Would you mind sharing what you were doing right before you noticed this feeling today? Sometimes these moments connect to small patterns in our daily flow.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Constant hum of worry. Some days, my mind looping over possible mistakes or what could go wrong at work; other days, it’s a restless energy that won’t settle, even when nothing urgent is happening. Sometimes, I´m motor running.'}]","Constant hum of worry. Some days, my mind looping over possible mistakes or what could go wrong at work; other days, it’s a restless energy that won’t settle, even when nothing urgent is happening. Sometimes, I´m motor running.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi there.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Robert, thanks for reaching out. I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Bad! Why do I feel wound up all the time, even when nothing´s actually wrong?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, I hear how frustrating that constant tension must feel - like your body\'s stuck in ""alert mode"" even when there\'s no real threat. Would you mind sharing what you were doing right before you noticed this feeling today? Sometimes these moments connect to small patterns in our daily flow.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Constant hum of worry. Some days, my mind looping over possible mistakes or what could go wrong at work; other days, it’s a restless energy that won’t settle, even when nothing urgent is happening. Sometimes, I´m motor running.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, that constant background hum of anxiety sounds incredibly draining - like your nervous system\'s stuck on standby even when there\'s no actual danger. When you describe it as ""motor running,"" I can almost feel that restless energy you\'re carrying. Could you share a recent moment when this feeling spiked unexpectedly? Sometimes noticing those triggers helps us find small entry points to ease the tension.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’ve started to notice how quickly the anxiety can hijack my focus, making it harder to be present with my family or follow through on plans. How do I stop running through the same ""what if"" thoughts on repeat, especially at night?'}]","I’ve started to notice how quickly the anxiety can hijack my focus, making it harder to be present with my family or follow through on plans. How do I stop running through the same ""what if"" thoughts on repeat, especially at night?",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi there.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Robert, thanks for reaching out. I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Bad! Why do I feel wound up all the time, even when nothing´s actually wrong?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, I hear how frustrating that constant tension must feel - like your body\'s stuck in ""alert mode"" even when there\'s no real threat. Would you mind sharing what you were doing right before you noticed this feeling today? Sometimes these moments connect to small patterns in our daily flow.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Constant hum of worry. Some days, my mind looping over possible mistakes or what could go wrong at work; other days, it’s a restless energy that won’t settle, even when nothing urgent is happening. Sometimes, I´m motor running.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, that constant background hum of anxiety sounds incredibly draining - like your nervous system\'s stuck on standby even when there\'s no actual danger. When you describe it as ""motor running,"" I can almost feel that restless energy you\'re carrying. Could you share a recent moment when this feeling spiked unexpectedly? Sometimes noticing those triggers helps us find small entry points to ease the tension.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’ve started to notice how quickly the anxiety can hijack my focus, making it harder to be present with my family or follow through on plans. How do I stop running through the same ""what if"" thoughts on repeat, especially at night?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, it makes complete sense that anxiety would pull you away from the present moment with your family - that constant ""what if"" loop must feel like a thief stealing your precious time. When you notice these thoughts starting at night, could you share what the very first sign is? Sometimes catching that first spark helps us find a way to gently redirect before the fire spreads.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My anxiety has been much harder to ignore. Even on nights when I get six or seven hours of sleep and mornings often start with hitting the snooze button more than once. Somedays, i just can´t face the day. Why?'}]","My anxiety has been much harder to ignore. Even on nights when I get six or seven hours of sleep and mornings often start with hitting the snooze button more than once. Somedays, i just can´t face the day. Why?",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': Hi there.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Hi Robert, thanks for reaching out. I\'m glad you\'re here. How are you feeling today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Bad! Why do I feel wound up all the time, even when nothing´s actually wrong?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, I hear how frustrating that constant tension must feel - like your body\'s stuck in ""alert mode"" even when there\'s no real threat. Would you mind sharing what you were doing right before you noticed this feeling today? Sometimes these moments connect to small patterns in our daily flow.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Constant hum of worry. Some days, my mind looping over possible mistakes or what could go wrong at work; other days, it’s a restless energy that won’t settle, even when nothing urgent is happening. Sometimes, I´m motor running.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, that constant background hum of anxiety sounds incredibly draining - like your nervous system\'s stuck on standby even when there\'s no actual danger. When you describe it as ""motor running,"" I can almost feel that restless energy you\'re carrying. Could you share a recent moment when this feeling spiked unexpectedly? Sometimes noticing those triggers helps us find small entry points to ease the tension.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I’ve started to notice how quickly the anxiety can hijack my focus, making it harder to be present with my family or follow through on plans. How do I stop running through the same ""what if"" thoughts on repeat, especially at night?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, it makes complete sense that anxiety would pull you away from the present moment with your family - that constant ""what if"" loop must feel like a thief stealing your precious time. When you notice these thoughts starting at night, could you share what the very first sign is? Sometimes catching that first spark helps us find a way to gently redirect before the fire spreads.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'My anxiety has been much harder to ignore. Even on nights when I get six or seven hours of sleep and mornings often start with hitting the snooze button more than once. Somedays, i just can´t face the day. Why?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Robert, it sounds like the weight of anxiety has become heavier lately, making mornings feel especially tough and days harder to start. I\'m wondering if there\'s a recent change in your routine or stressors that might be contributing to this shift? Sometimes even small adjustments can help lighten the load.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I keep waking up in the middle of the night with my chest feeling tight — like I could die. Is that anxiety, or something more serious?'}]","I keep waking up in the middle of the night with my chest feeling tight — like I could die. Is that anxiety, or something more serious?",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
