ent': 'I start feeling crunched for time and I don\'t enjoy it like I usually do. And things looks more contrived'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how unsettling it is when your work starts feeling rushed and disconnected from your authentic voice. When you notice this shift, what\'s one thing you notice in your own emotions that tells you this isn\'t the creative space you usually feel at home in?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'ANXIETY it\'s calling me. Have you heard Doechii\'s song Anxiety? It\'s great'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': That song seems to capture something powerful about anxiety—what part of it resonates with you?}, {'role': user, 'content': She talks about her experience with anxiety and she makes art from it}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It\'s powerful how you see anxiety as fuel for your art, like Doechii does. I\'m curious—when does that ""fuel"" start feeling more like a weight than a spark for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Kind of like I described earlier - the style shift, the time pressure'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'When that weight takes over, how does your relationship with the anxiety shift—does it feel more like a partner or a stranger taking the wheel?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Interesting -- a stranger. Maybe I\'ll make a piece about that!'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s such a thoughtful way to work through it. I\'m curious what you might discover about that ""stranger"" when you give it form through your art.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Me too. but I can\'t do that today. got to start packing up for the fair. Which I am a bit anxious about. It\'s always a lot to manage. Making sure I pack everything. Loading, unloading, setting up the booth. Making it look perfectly me. Getting a comfy chair because i\'ll be there all day. Making sure I have snacks. Hoping the weather cooperates. It\'s supposed to rain today so that\'s not great. Ans hoping I make sales but worrying no one will want to buy 