lready doing - like how the counter feels under your fingertips - but applied it to something that might help you right now, like noticing your feet on the floor?'}, {'role': user, 'content': ok whatever}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Nancy, I hear how frustrating this feels. What if we tried just one tiny thing together: as you look at your phone, notice how the counter feels under your fingertips for just 5 seconds? It\'s not about mindfulness - it\'s about giving your hands a small task while you wait.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'cold, hard -- granite'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really helpful to notice - the cold granite is a steady, reliable thing right there with you. What if we used this as a tiny anchor for just 10 seconds: while you wait for Mark\'s text, just keep noticing how that granite feels under your fingertips? It might help create a small pocket of calm in the waiting.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'He\'s never gonna text me back'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I hear how heavy that thought feels right now. What if we noticed together how your body responds when you think ""He\'s never gonna text me back""? Just for a moment, what does that thought do to your shoulders or your breath?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'my shoulders feel tight and i\'m holding my breath a bit'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That tightness and shallow breathing is your body\'s way of saying it needs relief right now. What if we used the counter to help you release some of that tension - like gently pressing your palms into it for just 5 seconds while you breathe out slowly? It might help melt that tightness.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'my shoulders feel tight and i\'m holding my breath a bit'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m noticing how your body is showing us the same pattern twice in a row - that tightness and shallow breathing. What if we saw that as your body trying to protect you, and your noticing it as a sign of how much you care a