"[{'role': user, 'content': 'So you\'re the AI that everyone\'s been talking about eh? Well if you\'re so smart maybe you can help me figure out some of my issues. I feel like a part of me lives in the past, in regret, in choices that I\'ve made earlier on in life that I wish I had made differently.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I\'m here to walk with you through these feelings of regret, but I can\'t solve them for you. What kinds of choices from your past are weighing on you most heavily right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I didn\'t ask you to solve them for me. Frankly that was presumptuous of you and I\'m not sure I want to speak to you'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I hear how important it is for you to have control over what we discuss. You\'re absolutely right that this is your journey, and I\'m here to walk alongside you at your pace. If you\'re willing, I\'d be glad to listen to what\'s weighing on you right now.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m a retired lawyer and I\'ve been fortunate to be successful in my career. But that success has come at a cost, and while at the time, I was willing to pay it, I now feel like I missed out on opportunities to be with family and loved ones that I can\'t get back and this haunts me a bit.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it makes sense that as you reflect on your career, you might notice moments where you prioritized work over family—those are the kinds of choices that can linger in our hearts. I\'m curious: when you think about those missed opportunities, what emotions come up for you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Regret. Sadness. Frustration. And some anger at myself. Strangely enough I also feel a bit angry at my parents for not preparing me or guiding me better to navigate life... but they were struggling to with dad\'s instability with work.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it sounds like these feelings carry a lot of weight—regret for missed moments, sadness about what’s past, and frustration that feels both personal and directed outward. I wonder how those emotions are showing up for you in your daily life right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Well, my kids are grown and have their own lives now... they call us every few weeks but a part of me feels like we would be closer now if I was more present with them when they were younger.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it makes sense that you\'d feel this way when reflecting on the past. I\'m curious: what does ""closer"" mean to you in terms of what you\'d like to experience with them now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'That is a good question. I suppose it would mean being more a part of each other\'s lives. Knowing the details of each other\'s lives and maintaining more regular contact'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, that desire to be more involved in their daily lives sounds meaningful. I\'m wondering what ""more"" might look like in your actual conversations - like, what kind of details would you like to know about them that you don\'t currently?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'d like to know how they are navigating life\'s difficult choices, career, family, values, religion. Our relationship feels very formal and topical so I don\'t really get to see those parts of their lives. And I also don\'t share those parts of myself because I don\'t want to make them uncomfortable. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I\'m noticing how your wish for deeper connection is being held back by a protective pattern you\'ve developed - one that likely served you well when you were building your career, but now might be preventing the closeness you\'re longing for. I wonder what might happen if you were to gently share even one small piece of what you\'re navigating, just to see how they respond?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Hmm.. like what?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, what about sharing a recent small moment that showed you how you\'re navigating something meaningful in your own life? Like, maybe how you\'re finding purpose in retirement or what you\'re learning from your dog. Just one tiny piece at a time.'}, {'role': user, 'content': I guess I could try sharing something small like that... I just wish that I put the time in when it mattered when they were younger... I was so stupid.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it\'s completely human to feel this way when reflecting on our past choices. I wonder if we could explore how to work with these feelings rather than against them, so you can find a different way forward.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t want to live in regret, but it is hard. I\'ll try what we talked about and will see if I can improve my relationship with my kids. But I\'m afraid of bothering them... I want to connect with them, partly because I feel like I\'m relying too much on my wife but I also don\'t want to be a burden.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it makes sense that you\'d worry about burdening others, but I\'m wondering if we could explore how small, authentic connections might actually help you feel less alone - even if it feels risky at first?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah I guess that makes sense. I wonder if feeling more connected will make me feel more motivated in general.. I haven\'t been too consistent with things like exercise these days.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it\'s interesting how you\'re noticing this connection between emotional connection and motivation. I wonder what might be making it hard to find that initial spark for exercise, even when you see how it could help?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It is just hard to care sometimes... I\'m old, my best days are behind me, and I\'m in that sunset phase of life where it\'s sort of like what\'s the point of working my ass off to live an extra 5 years '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it takes real courage to even consider small steps when you\'re feeling this way - that\'s a sign of your strength, not your weakness. I wonder if we could explore what would make those small moments of connection feel meaningful enough to sustain, even if they\'re just 5 minutes at a time?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Maybe if I felt like they were reciprocated. I know my kids are busy but it would be nice if they called me more often.}]",Maybe if I felt like they were reciprocated. I know my kids are busy but it would be nice if they called me more often.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'So you\'re the AI that everyone\'s been talking about eh? Well if you\'re so smart maybe you can help me figure out some of my issues. I feel like a part of me lives in the past, in regret, in choices that I\'ve made earlier on in life that I wish I had made differently.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I\'m here to walk with you through these feelings of regret, but I can\'t solve them for you. What kinds of choices from your past are weighing on you most heavily right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I didn\'t ask you to solve them for me. Frankly that was presumptuous of you and I\'m not sure I want to speak to you'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I hear how important it is for you to have control over what we discuss. You\'re absolutely right that this is your journey, and I\'m here to walk alongside you at your pace. If you\'re willing, I\'d be glad to listen to what\'s weighing on you right now.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m a retired lawyer and I\'ve been fortunate to be successful in my career. But that success has come at a cost, and while at the time, I was willing to pay it, I now feel like I missed out on opportunities to be with family and loved ones that I can\'t get back and this haunts me a bit.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it makes sense that as you reflect on your career, you might notice moments where you prioritized work over family—those are the kinds of choices that can linger in our hearts. I\'m curious: when you think about those missed opportunities, what emotions come up for you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Regret. Sadness. Frustration. And some anger at myself. Strangely enough I also feel a bit angry at my parents for not preparing me or guiding me better to navigate life... but they were struggling to with dad\'s instability with work.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it sounds like these feelings carry a lot of weight—regret for missed moments, sadness about what’s past, and frustration that feels both personal and directed outward. I wonder how those emotions are showing up for you in your daily life right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Well, my kids are grown and have their own lives now... they call us every few weeks but a part of me feels like we would be closer now if I was more present with them when they were younger.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it makes sense that you\'d feel this way when reflecting on the past. I\'m curious: what does ""closer"" mean to you in terms of what you\'d like to experience with them now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'That is a good question. I suppose it would mean being more a part of each other\'s lives. Knowing the details of each other\'s lives and maintaining more regular contact'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, that desire to be more involved in their daily lives sounds meaningful. I\'m wondering what ""more"" might look like in your actual conversations - like, what kind of details would you like to know about them that you don\'t currently?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'d like to know how they are navigating life\'s difficult choices, career, family, values, religion. Our relationship feels very formal and topical so I don\'t really get to see those parts of their lives. And I also don\'t share those parts of myself because I don\'t want to make them uncomfortable. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I\'m noticing how your wish for deeper connection is being held back by a protective pattern you\'ve developed - one that likely served you well when you were building your career, but now might be preventing the closeness you\'re longing for. I wonder what might happen if you were to gently share even one small piece of what you\'re navigating, just to see how they respond?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Hmm.. like what?}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, what about sharing a recent small moment that showed you how you\'re navigating something meaningful in your own life? Like, maybe how you\'re finding purpose in retirement or what you\'re learning from your dog. Just one tiny piece at a time.'}, {'role': user, 'content': I guess I could try sharing something small like that... I just wish that I put the time in when it mattered when they were younger... I was so stupid.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it\'s completely human to feel this way when reflecting on our past choices. I wonder if we could explore how to work with these feelings rather than against them, so you can find a different way forward.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t want to live in regret, but it is hard. I\'ll try what we talked about and will see if I can improve my relationship with my kids. But I\'m afraid of bothering them... I want to connect with them, partly because I feel like I\'m relying too much on my wife but I also don\'t want to be a burden.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it makes sense that you\'d worry about burdening others, but I\'m wondering if we could explore how small, authentic connections might actually help you feel less alone - even if it feels risky at first?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah I guess that makes sense. I wonder if feeling more connected will make me feel more motivated in general.. I haven\'t been too consistent with things like exercise these days.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it\'s interesting how you\'re noticing this connection between emotional connection and motivation. I wonder what might be making it hard to find that initial spark for exercise, even when you see how it could help?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It is just hard to care sometimes... I\'m old, my best days are behind me, and I\'m in that sunset phase of life where it\'s sort of like what\'s the point of working my ass off to live an extra 5 years '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, it takes real courage to even consider small steps when you\'re feeling this way - that\'s a sign of your strength, not your weakness. I wonder if we could explore what would make those small moments of connection feel meaningful enough to sustain, even if they\'re just 5 minutes at a time?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Maybe if I felt like they were reciprocated. I know my kids are busy but it would be nice if they called me more often.}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jacob, I hear how much you\'re hoping for that sense of being seen and valued in those moments. What would it mean to you if you could feel that connection, even without more frequent calls?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I guess I would feel like I am important to them and that would give me something of a sense of purpose. '}]",I guess I would feel like I am important to them and that would give me something of a sense of purpose. ,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.'}]",I don't feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how heavy this demotivation feels, especially when it’s also tangled up with your sleep struggles. Could you share a bit about how these two aspects are showing up in your day-to-day? For instance, do you notice when the fatigue from poor sleep makes it harder to start things, or does the lack of motivation somehow worsen your ability to rest?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up most nights at like 3 am and it takes me 1-2 hours to fall back asleep. I\'m so exhausted in the morning that it is hard to do anything, I feel like a robot... I don\'t have any motivation'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how draining that cycle must be—waking up exhausted and feeling disconnected. Could you share a specific morning challenge you’ve faced, like struggling with a work task or noticing how you react emotionally when you’re not at your best? That might help us spot small ways to ease the strain.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have to lead meetings in the morning and instead of inspiring my staff and focusing on student needs, I just try to get through it as fast as possible and steer away from talking about anything sensitive because my feelings are basically turned off'}]","I have to lead meetings in the morning and instead of inspiring my staff and focusing on student needs, I just try to get through it as fast as possible and steer away from talking about anything sensitive because my feelings are basically turned off",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how heavy this demotivation feels, especially when it’s also tangled up with your sleep struggles. Could you share a bit about how these two aspects are showing up in your day-to-day? For instance, do you notice when the fatigue from poor sleep makes it harder to start things, or does the lack of motivation somehow worsen your ability to rest?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up most nights at like 3 am and it takes me 1-2 hours to fall back asleep. I\'m so exhausted in the morning that it is hard to do anything, I feel like a robot... I don\'t have any motivation'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how draining that cycle must be—waking up exhausted and feeling disconnected. Could you share a specific morning challenge you’ve faced, like struggling with a work task or noticing how you react emotionally when you’re not at your best? That might help us spot small ways to ease the strain.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have to lead meetings in the morning and instead of inspiring my staff and focusing on student needs, I just try to get through it as fast as possible and steer away from talking about anything sensitive because my feelings are basically turned off'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I can hear how tough it is to show up for your staff when you\'re feeling so emotionally drained. Could you imagine a tiny way to reconnect with the reason you care about this work, even if it\'s just for a few minutes each morning? That might help you feel more grounded in the moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Not really... not when I\'m this tired every morning... I basically spend 2 hours trying to fall asleep and then another 2 hours trying to fall back asleep. I wonder if i should just get up at 3 am even though I\'m exhausted'}]",Not really... not when I'm this tired every morning... I basically spend 2 hours trying to fall asleep and then another 2 hours trying to fall back asleep. I wonder if i should just get up at 3 am even though I'm exhausted,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how heavy this demotivation feels, especially when it’s also tangled up with your sleep struggles. Could you share a bit about how these two aspects are showing up in your day-to-day? For instance, do you notice when the fatigue from poor sleep makes it harder to start things, or does the lack of motivation somehow worsen your ability to rest?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up most nights at like 3 am and it takes me 1-2 hours to fall back asleep. I\'m so exhausted in the morning that it is hard to do anything, I feel like a robot... I don\'t have any motivation'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how draining that cycle must be—waking up exhausted and feeling disconnected. Could you share a specific morning challenge you’ve faced, like struggling with a work task or noticing how you react emotionally when you’re not at your best? That might help us spot small ways to ease the strain.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have to lead meetings in the morning and instead of inspiring my staff and focusing on student needs, I just try to get through it as fast as possible and steer away from talking about anything sensitive because my feelings are basically turned off'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I can hear how tough it is to show up for your staff when you\'re feeling so emotionally drained. Could you imagine a tiny way to reconnect with the reason you care about this work, even if it\'s just for a few minutes each morning? That might help you feel more grounded in the moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Not really... not when I\'m this tired every morning... I basically spend 2 hours trying to fall asleep and then another 2 hours trying to fall back asleep. I wonder if i should just get up at 3 am even though I\'m exhausted'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how overwhelming this feels, and I want to gently point out that getting up at 3 a.m. might actually make things harder for your body and mind. What if we tried a tiny experiment together: instead of forcing yourself to stay awake, you could set a timer for 10 minutes of quiet presence—maybe just noticing your breath or the quiet in the room. Would that feel doable, even if it’s just for one morning?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah I know it is too early...  I mean 5 am would be ok, but 3 is peak night and not feasible. I\'ll try getting out of bed but I don\'t know what ""quiet presence"" means and I\'m not into that new agey mindfulness stuff.'}]","Yeah I know it is too early...  I mean 5 am would be ok, but 3 is peak night and not feasible. I'll try getting out of bed but I don't know what ""quiet presence"" means and I'm not into that new agey mindfulness stuff.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how heavy this demotivation feels, especially when it’s also tangled up with your sleep struggles. Could you share a bit about how these two aspects are showing up in your day-to-day? For instance, do you notice when the fatigue from poor sleep makes it harder to start things, or does the lack of motivation somehow worsen your ability to rest?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up most nights at like 3 am and it takes me 1-2 hours to fall back asleep. I\'m so exhausted in the morning that it is hard to do anything, I feel like a robot... I don\'t have any motivation'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how draining that cycle must be—waking up exhausted and feeling disconnected. Could you share a specific morning challenge you’ve faced, like struggling with a work task or noticing how you react emotionally when you’re not at your best? That might help us spot small ways to ease the strain.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have to lead meetings in the morning and instead of inspiring my staff and focusing on student needs, I just try to get through it as fast as possible and steer away from talking about anything sensitive because my feelings are basically turned off'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I can hear how tough it is to show up for your staff when you\'re feeling so emotionally drained. Could you imagine a tiny way to reconnect with the reason you care about this work, even if it\'s just for a few minutes each morning? That might help you feel more grounded in the moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Not really... not when I\'m this tired every morning... I basically spend 2 hours trying to fall asleep and then another 2 hours trying to fall back asleep. I wonder if i should just get up at 3 am even though I\'m exhausted'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how overwhelming this feels, and I want to gently point out that getting up at 3 a.m. might actually make things harder for your body and mind. What if we tried a tiny experiment together: instead of forcing yourself to stay awake, you could set a timer for 10 minutes of quiet presence—maybe just noticing your breath or the quiet in the room. Would that feel doable, even if it’s just for one morning?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah I know it is too early...  I mean 5 am would be ok, but 3 is peak night and not feasible. I\'ll try getting out of bed but I don\'t know what ""quiet presence"" means and I\'m not into that new agey mindfulness stuff.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how you want something practical, not abstract. What if we tried a tiny experiment: when you wake up at 3 a.m., you could set a timer for 10 minutes and just check the time quietly on your phone—no need to focus on anything else. That way, you\'re doing something concrete while avoiding the pressure to ""be present"" in a way that feels unfamiliar. Would that feel doable for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'That sounds terrible, honestly. It feels like you are trying to trick me into meditating without calling it that and I don\'t want to do it. I\'d rather read or something'}]","That sounds terrible, honestly. It feels like you are trying to trick me into meditating without calling it that and I don't want to do it. I'd rather read or something",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I don\'t feel motivated anymore and it is affecting my life... and my sleep.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how heavy this demotivation feels, especially when it’s also tangled up with your sleep struggles. Could you share a bit about how these two aspects are showing up in your day-to-day? For instance, do you notice when the fatigue from poor sleep makes it harder to start things, or does the lack of motivation somehow worsen your ability to rest?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I wake up most nights at like 3 am and it takes me 1-2 hours to fall back asleep. I\'m so exhausted in the morning that it is hard to do anything, I feel like a robot... I don\'t have any motivation'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how draining that cycle must be—waking up exhausted and feeling disconnected. Could you share a specific morning challenge you’ve faced, like struggling with a work task or noticing how you react emotionally when you’re not at your best? That might help us spot small ways to ease the strain.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have to lead meetings in the morning and instead of inspiring my staff and focusing on student needs, I just try to get through it as fast as possible and steer away from talking about anything sensitive because my feelings are basically turned off'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I can hear how tough it is to show up for your staff when you\'re feeling so emotionally drained. Could you imagine a tiny way to reconnect with the reason you care about this work, even if it\'s just for a few minutes each morning? That might help you feel more grounded in the moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Not really... not when I\'m this tired every morning... I basically spend 2 hours trying to fall asleep and then another 2 hours trying to fall back asleep. I wonder if i should just get up at 3 am even though I\'m exhausted'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how overwhelming this feels, and I want to gently point out that getting up at 3 a.m. might actually make things harder for your body and mind. What if we tried a tiny experiment together: instead of forcing yourself to stay awake, you could set a timer for 10 minutes of quiet presence—maybe just noticing your breath or the quiet in the room. Would that feel doable, even if it’s just for one morning?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah I know it is too early...  I mean 5 am would be ok, but 3 is peak night and not feasible. I\'ll try getting out of bed but I don\'t know what ""quiet presence"" means and I\'m not into that new agey mindfulness stuff.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how you want something practical, not abstract. What if we tried a tiny experiment: when you wake up at 3 a.m., you could set a timer for 10 minutes and just check the time quietly on your phone—no need to focus on anything else. That way, you\'re doing something concrete while avoiding the pressure to ""be present"" in a way that feels unfamiliar. Would that feel doable for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'That sounds terrible, honestly. It feels like you are trying to trick me into meditating without calling it that and I don\'t want to do it. I\'d rather read or something'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear you - that\'s a valid concern, and I want to respect what works for you. What if we tried a tiny adjustment: when you wake up, you could just read one page of something you enjoy (no pressure to read more), and then put the book down after that. It\'s still a small break from lying awake, but it\'s something familiar that doesn\'t feel like meditation. Would that feel more doable for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah I\'ll do that... but not a single page because that is like 30 seconds and that won\'t do anything... I\'ll read for like 10-15 minutes and try to sleep again'}]",Yeah I'll do that... but not a single page because that is like 30 seconds and that won't do anything... I'll read for like 10-15 minutes and try to sleep again,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
