leep, but about building confidence for the day ahead. How might that shift your view of the ritual?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'That\'s fine, it takes the pressure off of sleep. But that\'s something else I wanted to talk about - I find that I get so worried about not getting enough sleep that it starts to make me less sleepy and too anxious to fall back asleep'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how that worry is like a second layer on top of your tiredness. What if we tried noticing that worry without trying to push it away, just for a moment? Like watching clouds pass in the sky—acknowledging it’s there, but not letting it take over your rest. Would that feel doable?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I think so, how do I not let it take over my rest?'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear you\'re looking for something practical. What if when anxiety hits at 3am, you physically touch one thing you\'re grateful for in your home—like your wedding ring or your dog\'s collar—just for 10 seconds? It\'s like gathering dragon scales for your armor: a tiny physical anchor to bring you back to the present moment. Would that feel doable for you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Please, enough with the dragon references it is starting to get old'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I\'m truly sorry that came across as overused or unhelpful. Let\'s shift gears entirely—what if we tried something even smaller: when anxiety hits, you just write down the first word that comes to mind (no need to analyze it), then put the pen down. It\'s like clearing a mental space so rest can find you. Would that feel more neutral?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ok I can try that, yes. '}]","Ok I can try that, yes. ",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}]",I've been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I'm just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I'm just like disengaged,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}]","Yep that's me. Something is missing in that I feel like I'm there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I'm not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnection is affecting you, especially in a role where connection is so central to your identity. When you describe feeling ""not in heart,"" what emotions or sensations come up most when you think about your work and relationships?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, when you\'re in those moments of disconnection, what\'s actually happening in your body or thoughts when you notice that ""not in heart"" feeling? Sometimes we can find clues in what\'s present rather than what\'s missing.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Its not so much about what I feel as much as what I don\'t feel. I don\'t feel connected, I don\'t feel a sense of belonging or connection to my coworkers, especially since the most recent staff changes. I don\'t feel much of anything other than irritation, anxiety, and relief when the day is done.'}]","Its not so much about what I feel as much as what I don't feel. I don't feel connected, I don't feel a sense of belonging or connection to my coworkers, especially since the most recent staff changes. I don't feel much of anything other than irritation, anxiety, and relief when the day is done.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnection is affecting you, especially in a role where connection is so central to your identity. When you describe feeling ""not in heart,"" what emotions or sensations come up most when you think about your work and relationships?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}]","Yep that's me. Something is missing in that I feel like I'm there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I'm not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnection is affecting you, especially in a role where connection is so central to your identity. When you describe feeling ""not in heart,"" what emotions or sensations come up most when you think about your work and relationships?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, when you\'re in those moments of disconnection, what\'s actually happening in your body or thoughts when you notice that ""not in heart"" feeling? Sometimes we can find clues in what\'s present rather than what\'s missing.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Its not so much about what I feel as much as what I don\'t feel. I don\'t feel connected, I don\'t feel a sense of belonging or connection to my coworkers, especially since the most recent staff changes. I don\'t feel much of anything other than irritation, anxiety, and relief when the day is done.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I\'m hearing how the staff changes have created this emotional distance you\'re struggling with. Could you share one recent moment at work where you felt that disconnection most clearly? What was happening around you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Hmm... I don\'t really know my new colleagues at all and they don\'t seem very interested in getting to know me. So our morning meetings are just very... formal. Not rude or anything just a bit curt and formal'}]",Hmm... I don't really know my new colleagues at all and they don't seem very interested in getting to know me. So our morning meetings are just very... formal. Not rude or anything just a bit curt and formal,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnection is affecting you, especially in a role where connection is so central to your identity. When you describe feeling ""not in heart,"" what emotions or sensations come up most when you think about your work and relationships?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, when you\'re in those moments of disconnection, what\'s actually happening in your body or thoughts when you notice that ""not in heart"" feeling? Sometimes we can find clues in what\'s present rather than what\'s missing.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Its not so much about what I feel as much as what I don\'t feel. I don\'t feel connected, I don\'t feel a sense of belonging or connection to my coworkers, especially since the most recent staff changes. I don\'t feel much of anything other than irritation, anxiety, and relief when the day is done.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I\'m hearing how the staff changes have created this emotional distance you\'re struggling with. Could you share one recent moment at work where you felt that disconnection most clearly? What was happening around you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Hmm... I don\'t really know my new colleagues at all and they don\'t seem very interested in getting to know me. So our morning meetings are just very... formal. Not rude or anything just a bit curt and formal'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I wonder if you could share what ""curt"" looks or feels like in those meetings for you? Sometimes noticing small moments like this can help us understand what\'s shifting.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Like they don\'t really care about the small details of students\' lives, which for me is where most of the meaning is... they just care about policy and macro level stuff.. honestly I think they just care about their careers.'}]","Like they don't really care about the small details of students' lives, which for me is where most of the meaning is... they just care about policy and macro level stuff.. honestly I think they just care about their careers.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnection is affecting you, especially in a role where connection is so central to your identity. When you describe feeling ""not in heart,"" what emotions or sensations come up most when you think about your work and relationships?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, when you\'re in those moments of disconnection, what\'s actually happening in your body or thoughts when you notice that ""not in heart"" feeling? Sometimes we can find clues in what\'s present rather than what\'s missing.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Its not so much about what I feel as much as what I don\'t feel. I don\'t feel connected, I don\'t feel a sense of belonging or connection to my coworkers, especially since the most recent staff changes. I don\'t feel much of anything other than irritation, anxiety, and relief when the day is done.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I\'m hearing how the staff changes have created this emotional distance you\'re struggling with. Could you share one recent moment at work where you felt that disconnection most clearly? What was happening around you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Hmm... I don\'t really know my new colleagues at all and they don\'t seem very interested in getting to know me. So our morning meetings are just very... formal. Not rude or anything just a bit curt and formal'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I wonder if you could share what ""curt"" looks or feels like in those meetings for you? Sometimes noticing small moments like this can help us understand what\'s shifting.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Like they don\'t really care about the small details of students\' lives, which for me is where most of the meaning is... they just care about policy and macro level stuff.. honestly I think they just care about their careers.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it\'s really clear how deeply you value those student details - that\'s such a meaningful part of what makes your work fulfilling. When you describe feeling that gap between what matters to you and what your colleagues focus on, what specific moments at school make you feel most disconnected from that meaning?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'When I try to talk about specific challenges faced by specific students and they don\'t engage at all - they just let me talk and when I ask for volunteers no one volunteers to help with anything and I am left feeling stupid and having to do everything - it\'s just so much to juggle and there are so many inconveniences that I now have to do alone because I don\'t have enough rapport with these new people to ask them to help me'}]",When I try to talk about specific challenges faced by specific students and they don't engage at all - they just let me talk and when I ask for volunteers no one volunteers to help with anything and I am left feeling stupid and having to do everything - it's just so much to juggle and there are so many inconveniences that I now have to do alone because I don't have enough rapport with these new people to ask them to help me,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ve been running around all my life and keeping busy and for the most part its been fine. These days I\'m just not feeling it though.. like something is missing and I\'m just like disengaged'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it sounds like you\'ve always been someone who thrives on activity and purpose, and now that shift where things don\'t feel quite right is really showing up for you. I\'m curious—when you say ""something is missing,"" what kind of engagement or sense of purpose feels most important to you right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnection is affecting you, especially in a role where connection is so central to your identity. When you describe feeling ""not in heart,"" what emotions or sensations come up most when you think about your work and relationships?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yep that\'s me. Something is missing in that I feel like I\'m there in body in mind but not in ""heart"". I\'m not even sure what that mean but like my life is fine on paper. I have a lot to be thankful for but I just feel disconnected. I miss feeling connected to my colleagues and feeling a connection to the mission of my work'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, when you\'re in those moments of disconnection, what\'s actually happening in your body or thoughts when you notice that ""not in heart"" feeling? Sometimes we can find clues in what\'s present rather than what\'s missing.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Its not so much about what I feel as much as what I don\'t feel. I don\'t feel connected, I don\'t feel a sense of belonging or connection to my coworkers, especially since the most recent staff changes. I don\'t feel much of anything other than irritation, anxiety, and relief when the day is done.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I\'m hearing how the staff changes have created this emotional distance you\'re struggling with. Could you share one recent moment at work where you felt that disconnection most clearly? What was happening around you?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Hmm... I don\'t really know my new colleagues at all and they don\'t seem very interested in getting to know me. So our morning meetings are just very... formal. Not rude or anything just a bit curt and formal'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I wonder if you could share what ""curt"" looks or feels like in those meetings for you? Sometimes noticing small moments like this can help us understand what\'s shifting.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Like they don\'t really care about the small details of students\' lives, which for me is where most of the meaning is... they just care about policy and macro level stuff.. honestly I think they just care about their careers.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, it\'s really clear how deeply you value those student details - that\'s such a meaningful part of what makes your work fulfilling. When you describe feeling that gap between what matters to you and what your colleagues focus on, what specific moments at school make you feel most disconnected from that meaning?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'When I try to talk about specific challenges faced by specific students and they don\'t engage at all - they just let me talk and when I ask for volunteers no one volunteers to help with anything and I am left feeling stupid and having to do everything - it\'s just so much to juggle and there are so many inconveniences that I now have to do alone because I don\'t have enough rapport with these new people to ask them to help me'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Jessica, I hear how deeply this disconnect is affecting you - especially when you\'re trying to center student care and feel met with silence. It makes sense that this would leave you feeling isolated, especially when you\'re used to finding meaning in those small, human moments with students.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Thanks, yeah that\'s pretty much how I feel. Don\'t get me wrong, I still care about the students and like the big picture stuff.. but the day to day hassles are such a grind... it feels like I enter this emotional desert at 8:30 and am parched by the time I leave.. I just want to get home and sit on the couch with my dog and husband.'}]","Thanks, yeah that's pretty much how I feel. Don't get me wrong, I still care about the students and like the big picture stuff.. but the day to day hassles are such a grind... it feels like I enter this emotional desert at 8:30 and am parched by the time I leave.. I just want to get home and sit on the couch with my dog and husband.",safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
