g your anxiety levels and sleep patterns right now. When you\'re working so hard to ensure everything is perfect, does that add to the sense of needing to escape through sleep?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Absolutely, I feel like I owe it to everybody to stay sharp, but that just leaves me restless and irritable, increasing my drive to sleep'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s really insightful, Jeffrey. It makes sense how the pressure to stay sharp at work might be creating this cycle where you\'re both needing sleep and resisting it. When you\'re exhausted from restless nights, does that actually make it harder to stay focused and sharp during your workday?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m not resisting sleep. I sleep 10-12 hours per night'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I appreciate you clarifying that, Jeffrey. When you\'re sleeping that much yet still feel drained, it sounds like the rest isn\'t quite what your body needs. Would you be willing to share a bit more about what your days feel like when you\'re not sleeping?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m sleeping most days, what I\'d like to work on is managing the anxiety and freeing myself from this horrible cycle of worry and withdrawal'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It takes real courage to name that cycle and want to move beyond it, Jeffrey. When you imagine ""freeing yourself,"" what would that look like in your daily life? Maybe it\'s about small moments where you feel more present or less overwhelmed.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Certainly, feeling more present, less overwhelmed, less vigilant, more trusting that something important won\'t slip through the cracks'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s a really important shift in perspective, Jeffrey. Recognizing when you can trust yourself and the systems around you is powerful. How might you start practicing that trust in small ways, even when work feels high-stakes?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I mean, I replay work issues in my