d frustration)'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It makes sense to feel that way when you\'re stepping away from work, especially with such high expectations. I\'m curious—when you think ""I haven\'t done enough,"" is that thought actually true, or does it feel like it might be magnifying the situation?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m an overachiever, alway have been, so it\'s possible i\'m over exaggerating the situation  but to me it feel like i\'m slacking  sometimes'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That self-awareness about potentially magnifying things is really important work. When you\'re lying there at 3am, what if you could gently remind yourself that ""enough"" doesn\'t mean ""perfect""? How might that change how you feel about those unfinished tasks?'}, {'role': user, 'content': hmm say more}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'When you notice that ""I haven\'t done enough"" thought, could you try whispering ""enough isn\'t perfect"" to yourself while taking one slow breath? How does that feel in your body compared to the tension you\'ve been noticing?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'wow, i like that, i\'m going to try that right now'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I\'m so glad you\'re willing to try it now. As you practice this, I\'m curious—does the tension in your body start to soften at all? And how does this feel connected to the big changes happening in your life right now?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'i didnt notice any changes in tension just now,but do feel more mentally calm when i say that, i\'ll need tom practice this alot '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That mental calm is a great sign—it often takes practice for the physical sensations to shift. I wonder if that calm feeling might be enough to help you drift back to sleep when you\'re lying there at 3am?'}, {'role': user, 'content': i very well could}]",i very well could,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
