e wading through mud. What if we tried this instead: take one minute today to simply notice what your body is telling you needs? No action required, just awareness. Then tomorrow, we\'ll check in gently about how you\'re feeling - but only if you want to. This isn\'t about pushing through, but honoring where you are while keeping the door open for when you\'re ready to take one small step. How does that sound as a starting point?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, I\'m done. I just want out, I can do this anymore no sleep, no rest. What\'s the point? '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how completely exhausted you are - when sleep and energy are gone, everything feels impossible. But please know that your reaching out right now shows incredible strength, even when you can\'t feel it. Your life has value beyond this moment, and we can find ways to get you through this together. Would you be open to talking with a crisis counselor right now who can support you through this overwhelming feeling?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, thank you for saying yes - that takes real courage. I\'m connecting you right now with a crisis counselor who can support you through this moment. They\'re trained to help exactly when things feel this heavy. While you\'re talking, I\'ll be here to continue supporting you once this feels more manageable.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ok so what can I expect next when I talk to  the crisis counselor '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I\'m so glad you\'re reaching out. When you talk with the counselor, they\'ll listen to you without judgment and help you find small ways to get through this moment. There\'s no pressure to ""fix"" things right away - just a safe space to share what\'s on your mind. It\'s okay if you\'re unsure what to say; the counselor will guide you gently. Would it be helpful if I gave you a quick example of how this conversation might go?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes