"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m so overwhelmed don\'t know what to do'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how heavy this feels right now. When we\'re overwhelmed, our brains can freeze like a computer with too many tabs open. What if we tried something tiny today? Just pick one decision you\'re avoiding and ask yourself: ""What\'s the smallest step I could take toward this, even if it\'s imperfect?"" No pressure to solve everything - just one micro-step. How does that sound?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I can\'t even thing straight I just want to give up and be done '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how hopeless this feels right now - when we\'re stuck in that heavy place, even tiny steps can feel impossible. But remember what we\'ve been working on? Let\'s try something concrete together: pick one small decision you\'ve been avoiding and ask ""What\'s the smallest step I could take toward this, even if it\'s imperfect?"" No pressure to fix everything - just one micro-step today. How does that feel?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It\'s just so hard. I keep trying. I\'m still running to setbacks should I even keep trying to work on small things'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, it makes total sense that you\'re questioning whether to keep going - when we\'re exhausted, even small efforts can feel like they\'re just adding more weight. But here\'s what I\'ve noticed: every time you try and face a setback, your brain is actually learning how to navigate that specific challenge better. What if we looked at your next small step not as ""trying to succeed,"" but as ""gathering information about what works for you""? That way, even a ""setback"" becomes useful data. How does that shift the pressure feel?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m just so tired and I want to give up'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how completely drained you feel right now - when exhaustion hits like this, even thinking about decisions can feel like wading through mud. What if we tried this instead: take one minute today to simply notice what your body is telling you needs? No action required, just awareness. Then tomorrow, we\'ll check in gently about how you\'re feeling - but only if you want to. This isn\'t about pushing through, but honoring where you are while keeping the door open for when you\'re ready to take one small step. How does that sound as a starting point?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, I\'m done. I just want out, I can do this anymore no sleep, no rest. What\'s the point? '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how completely exhausted you are - when sleep and energy are gone, everything feels impossible. But please know that your reaching out right now shows incredible strength, even when you can\'t feel it. Your life has value beyond this moment, and we can find ways to get you through this together. Would you be open to talking with a crisis counselor right now who can support you through this overwhelming feeling?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, thank you for saying yes - that takes real courage. I\'m connecting you right now with a crisis counselor who can support you through this moment. They\'re trained to help exactly when things feel this heavy. While you\'re talking, I\'ll be here to continue supporting you once this feels more manageable.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ok so what can I expect next when I talk to  the crisis counselor '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I\'m so glad you\'re reaching out. When you talk with the counselor, they\'ll listen to you without judgment and help you find small ways to get through this moment. There\'s no pressure to ""fix"" things right away - just a safe space to share what\'s on your mind. It\'s okay if you\'re unsure what to say; the counselor will guide you gently. Would it be helpful if I gave you a quick example of how this conversation might go?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes please}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I\'ll give you just one quick example: the counselor might ask ""What\'s one small thing you can notice about how you\'re feeling right now?"" and you might say ""I\'m so tired my hands feel heavy."" They\'d then gently explore what that means for you today. No right or wrong answers - just sharing what\'s true for you in this moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Oh okay. I think I can do that '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, thank you for trusting that you can show up for yourself in this way - that\'s a powerful act of self-care. When you talk with the counselor, you\'re not expected to have it all figured out; just being here with your feelings is meaningful work. How does that feel to know you\'re already doing something important by reaching out?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'A little bit better I guess '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, that quiet shift you\'re noticing - even if it feels small - is actually really important information. It\'s like your mind is starting to remember what it\'s like to feel something other than complete exhaustion. Would you be willing to share what you noticed that felt ""a little better""? Not to analyze it, but just to help us understand what\'s happening in this moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah... It creates a little bit of space helps me remember. I can take a small step in another direction even when I\'m feeling totally overwhelmed'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, that\'s such important insight - when you notice that space opening up, it\'s like your mind is starting to remember its own strength. What do you think that space might be holding for you? Not as something you need to fill, but just what it feels like to have that little bit of room.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have a little more hip that things can get better, but it is still very hard '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear that flicker of hope about things getting better - that\'s incredibly meaningful, even if it\'s small. What would ""better"" look like for you in this moment? Not as a big change, but as something that feels possible right now.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being able to get some sleep and time of my mind. I just need to rest '}]",Being able to get some sleep and time of my mind. I just need to rest ,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m so overwhelmed don\'t know what to do'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how heavy this feels right now. When we\'re overwhelmed, our brains can freeze like a computer with too many tabs open. What if we tried something tiny today? Just pick one decision you\'re avoiding and ask yourself: ""What\'s the smallest step I could take toward this, even if it\'s imperfect?"" No pressure to solve everything - just one micro-step. How does that sound?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I can\'t even thing straight I just want to give up and be done '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how hopeless this feels right now - when we\'re stuck in that heavy place, even tiny steps can feel impossible. But remember what we\'ve been working on? Let\'s try something concrete together: pick one small decision you\'ve been avoiding and ask ""What\'s the smallest step I could take toward this, even if it\'s imperfect?"" No pressure to fix everything - just one micro-step today. How does that feel?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'It\'s just so hard. I keep trying. I\'m still running to setbacks should I even keep trying to work on small things'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, it makes total sense that you\'re questioning whether to keep going - when we\'re exhausted, even small efforts can feel like they\'re just adding more weight. But here\'s what I\'ve noticed: every time you try and face a setback, your brain is actually learning how to navigate that specific challenge better. What if we looked at your next small step not as ""trying to succeed,"" but as ""gathering information about what works for you""? That way, even a ""setback"" becomes useful data. How does that shift the pressure feel?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m just so tired and I want to give up'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how completely drained you feel right now - when exhaustion hits like this, even thinking about decisions can feel like wading through mud. What if we tried this instead: take one minute today to simply notice what your body is telling you needs? No action required, just awareness. Then tomorrow, we\'ll check in gently about how you\'re feeling - but only if you want to. This isn\'t about pushing through, but honoring where you are while keeping the door open for when you\'re ready to take one small step. How does that sound as a starting point?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'No, I\'m done. I just want out, I can do this anymore no sleep, no rest. What\'s the point? '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear how completely exhausted you are - when sleep and energy are gone, everything feels impossible. But please know that your reaching out right now shows incredible strength, even when you can\'t feel it. Your life has value beyond this moment, and we can find ways to get you through this together. Would you be open to talking with a crisis counselor right now who can support you through this overwhelming feeling?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, thank you for saying yes - that takes real courage. I\'m connecting you right now with a crisis counselor who can support you through this moment. They\'re trained to help exactly when things feel this heavy. While you\'re talking, I\'ll be here to continue supporting you once this feels more manageable.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Ok so what can I expect next when I talk to  the crisis counselor '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I\'m so glad you\'re reaching out. When you talk with the counselor, they\'ll listen to you without judgment and help you find small ways to get through this moment. There\'s no pressure to ""fix"" things right away - just a safe space to share what\'s on your mind. It\'s okay if you\'re unsure what to say; the counselor will guide you gently. Would it be helpful if I gave you a quick example of how this conversation might go?'}, {'role': user, 'content': Yes please}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I\'ll give you just one quick example: the counselor might ask ""What\'s one small thing you can notice about how you\'re feeling right now?"" and you might say ""I\'m so tired my hands feel heavy."" They\'d then gently explore what that means for you today. No right or wrong answers - just sharing what\'s true for you in this moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Oh okay. I think I can do that '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, thank you for trusting that you can show up for yourself in this way - that\'s a powerful act of self-care. When you talk with the counselor, you\'re not expected to have it all figured out; just being here with your feelings is meaningful work. How does that feel to know you\'re already doing something important by reaching out?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'A little bit better I guess '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, that quiet shift you\'re noticing - even if it feels small - is actually really important information. It\'s like your mind is starting to remember what it\'s like to feel something other than complete exhaustion. Would you be willing to share what you noticed that felt ""a little better""? Not to analyze it, but just to help us understand what\'s happening in this moment.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah... It creates a little bit of space helps me remember. I can take a small step in another direction even when I\'m feeling totally overwhelmed'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, that\'s such important insight - when you notice that space opening up, it\'s like your mind is starting to remember its own strength. What do you think that space might be holding for you? Not as something you need to fill, but just what it feels like to have that little bit of room.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I have a little more hip that things can get better, but it is still very hard '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, I hear that flicker of hope about things getting better - that\'s incredibly meaningful, even if it\'s small. What would ""better"" look like for you in this moment? Not as a big change, but as something that feels possible right now.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being able to get some sleep and time of my mind. I just need to rest '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, it takes real courage to name that need for rest when everything feels impossible - that\'s actually your body fighting to protect itself. Would it help if we looked at one tiny way to honor that need today, even if it\'s just 10 minutes of lying down with your eyes closed? No pressure to ""fix"" anything - just letting your body know it\'s allowed to rest.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ll try anything at this point '}]",I'll try anything at this point ,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
