 better - that\'s incredibly meaningful, even if it\'s small. What would ""better"" look like for you in this moment? Not as a big change, but as something that feels possible right now.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Being able to get some sleep and time of my mind. I just need to rest '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, it takes real courage to name that need for rest when everything feels impossible - that\'s actually your body fighting to protect itself. Would it help if we looked at one tiny way to honor that need today, even if it\'s just 10 minutes of lying down with your eyes closed? No pressure to ""fix"" anything - just letting your body know it\'s allowed to rest.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ll try anything at this point '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'Lisa, thank you for trusting this process with me - that willingness to try is such a gift. What if we made it super small: just 5 minutes of lying down with your eyes closed today, with no expectation of sleep? Just noticing how your body feels in that moment. No pressure to do more than that - it\'s just an experiment to see what your body might need. How does that feel as a starting point?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ll try. What should I do if I\'m feeling so overwhelmed again to the point of not having any hope?'}]",I'll try. What should I do if I'm feeling so overwhelmed again to the point of not having any hope?,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
