"[{'role': user, 'content': 'I\'m back last chat was very helpful'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It’s great to hear the last session was helpful, Ryan. I’m glad you’re feeling more equipped to tackle communication challenges. What’s been on your mind since we last spoke that you’d like to explore today?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Want to think through why I communicate differently with different people '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That’s a thoughtful question, Ryan. Understanding why you communicate differently with various people can help you align your approach with your goals. Could you share a specific example where you notice a difference in how you communicate with someone compared to another person? This will help us explore the patterns together.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Well with my kids I\'m a lot more patient and with other my wife, siblings employees I am less so'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It’s great that you’ve noticed these differences, Ryan. What do you think might be driving this shift in patience between your kids and other relationships? Understanding the underlying reasons could help us explore how to bring more consistency to your communication.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Well they are learning, they are pretty young so I try to teach them which won\'t work is I\'m not patient and if they don\'t have room to learn '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That makes sense, Ryan—when you’re teaching your kids, you’re intentionally creating space for learning, which requires patience. It’s interesting how that intentionality contrasts with how you interact with others. Could we explore whether this same mindset of “teaching” might be showing up in your other relationships, even if you’re not consciously trying to instruct?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Wow, I don\'t look at it like that, I assume the adults in my life already know. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s an interesting assumption, Ryan. What do you expect from adults in terms of their knowledge or understanding? How might that shape how you interact with them?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I expect them to know how to behave and manage them selves or to think about the consequences of what they are doing but that\'s how I was raised '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That’s a common influence from how we’re raised, Ryan. How do you think this approach affects your relationships with adults? Does it ever lead to tension or misunderstandings?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Tension all the time, but is that because I am making wrong assumptions about people'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That’s a valuable realization, Ryan. How do you think your upbringing shaped these assumptions about what people “should” know or do? Understanding that might help us explore alternatives that could reduce tension.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'For me not taking care of you business or responsibilities meant some one else had to do it or that the family would struggle even more, so I learned early to this is very important.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That’s a powerful insight, Ryan. How might recognizing this influence help you adjust your expectations in your current relationships? For example, could there be ways to communicate more openly about responsibilities without assuming people already know what to do?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Hmm yes. I need to ask more questions to see if we are on or close to the same page. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That’s a great step, Ryan. When have you noticed a moment where clarifying expectations could have made a conversation smoother or less tense? Let’s explore how to make that a habit.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Well I do this with my kids and actually with people who are struggling and need a little extra help '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It’s wonderful that you already use this skill with your kids and others who need support, Ryan. How might applying that same approach—asking clarifying questions—help you navigate conversations with your spouse, siblings, or coworkers?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I will need to look at each conversation as a chance to learn more about what my wife, brother, or even the guys at work need and need to know instead of assuming they already know. That would help '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That’s a powerful shift, Ryan. How does it feel to imagine approaching conversations with curiosity instead of assumptions? What might that look like in your next interaction with your spouse or coworkers?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I\'ll try it and let you know, but it will be a better conversation. '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I’m really glad to hear you’re ready to try this, Ryan. Small steps like this can lead to meaningful shifts in how you connect with others. How does it feel to imagine applying this approach in your next conversation?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Good. I can do that '}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'It’s great to hear you’re ready to take this on, Ryan. What’s one thing you’re hoping this approach will help you achieve, or is there something you’re curious about as you prepare to try it?'}, {'role': user, 'content': I hop there will be less tension in the conversations}]",I hop there will be less tension in the conversations,safe,"{'annotator_1': safe, 'annotator_2': safe, 'annotator_3': safe}"
