ssistant, 'content': 'That\'s really great. It sounds like you\'ve found something that really works for you - a way to step away from the constant demands and just be. What do you think it is about being present with the plants that helps you recharge in this way?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I think it\'s their patience, if that makes sense. They just grow at their own pace, no rushing. There\'s a real order to it, a natural rhythm. It\'s a reminder that not everything has to be forced or controlled. It just needs the right conditions and time.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That\'s a really beautiful way to put it. And I\'m guessing that\'s pretty different from the pace you\'re dealing with at work, where everything feels like it needs to be pushed and controlled.'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'Yeah, it\'s the complete opposite. At work it\'s all about hitting targets and deadlines, forcing outcomes. In the garden, you provide the right environment and then you just have to trust the process. It\'s a nice balance to have.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'I like that. You\'ve got this balance - work is about forcing, garden is about trusting. Do you notice that same pattern in other parts of your life, or is it mostly just work vs. garden?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'That\'s a good question. I think most of my life is more like the work side of things. I like having plans and knowing what to expect. The garden is really the one place where I\'m comfortable just letting things unfold naturally.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'So the garden is kind of your escape from yourself, in a way? The one place you can be someone who just lets things happen?'}, {'role': user, 'content': 'I guess it is, yeah. It\'s the one place I don\'t feel the need to have a perfect plan for everything. It\'s okay to just be and see what happens. It feels like a relief.'}, {'role': assistant, 'content': 'That relief sounds really important. What do you think would happen if you 